{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HeckeCompletion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HeckeCompletion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.HeckeGS"],"declarations":940,"chunks":2},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompleted_threading_cost_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompleted_threading_cost_unique","kind":"theorem","line":18809,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18809-L18819","doc":"**Threading cost is well-defined** — with no hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompleted_normalForm_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompleted_normalForm_unique","kind":"theorem","line":18795,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18795-L18807","doc":"**Normal forms in the completed Hecke system are unique** — with no\nhypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompleted_rules_lc_isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompleted_rules_lc_isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":18781,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18781-L18793","doc":"**Every rule of the completed Hecke system has a unit leading\ncoefficient** (`±1`). This is the hypothesis `local_confluence` carries since\n2026-11-15. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompleted_isGrobnerShirshovBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompleted_isGrobnerShirshovBasis","kind":"theorem","line":18737,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18737-L18745","doc":"**The completed Hecke rewriting system is a Gröbner–Shirshov basis** — with\nno hypothesis left. `deep_selfOverlap_resolves` discharges the `hdeep` the\nconditional form carried. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.deep_selfOverlap_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.deep_selfOverlap_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":18582,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18582-L18735","doc":"**The deep self-overlap resolves** — the last obligation of\n`heckeCompleted_isGrobnerShirshovBasis`.\n\nThe S-polynomial is two terms, `left · bsWord₂` and `bsWord₂ · right`, the\n`bsWord₁` placements having cancelled. Side A runs on the first with the second\nas context, side B then on the second with side A's normal form as context, and\nthe two normal forms coincide — so the four terms cancel in pairs.\n\nNothing here needs the two sides not to collide. `isZero` is coefficientwise and\n`ofTerms` sums, so terms sharing a word simply add; and a step's side condition\nconstrains the word it *consumes*, never the word it produces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.deep_left_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.deep_left_right","kind":"theorem","line":18548,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18548-L18580","doc":"**The deep self-overlap's contexts are forced.**\n\n`σ_a σ_{a−1} ⋯ σ₀ σ_a` has exactly one border once `a ≥ 1`: the single letter\n`σ_a`. Any longer border of length `k` would need its first letter `σ_a` to\nequal the suffix's first letter `σ_{k−2}`, which happens only at the full word —\nand `left ≠ []` excludes that. `overlap_letter` already does the length-one\nwork; what is left is reading `left` and `right` off the two decompositions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ctxAvoids_tail_of_last_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ctxAvoids_tail_of_last_ne","kind":"theorem","line":18531,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18531-L18546","doc":"A context whose words all end in `x` avoids every pattern ending in a\ndifferent letter `y`. This is the *tail* condition side B's unshuffle needs,\nand a last-letter comparison is all it takes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ctxAvoids_head_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ctxAvoids_head_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":18524,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18524-L18529","doc":"A context whose words never begin with `x` avoids `x` as a head. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.selfOverlap_spoly_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.selfOverlap_spoly_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":18485,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18485-L18522","doc":"**The S-polynomial of a self-overlap by a monic two-word rule.**\n\n`spoly = lc₂ • (rule₁ · right) − lc₁ • (left · rule₂)`, and when both rules are\nthe same monic `L − R` the two `L`-terms are the *same word*: `L ++ right =\nleft ++ overlap ++ right = left ++ L`. What is left is the difference of the two\n`R`-placements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":18435,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18435-L18449","doc":"**Side B of the deep self-overlap resolves, in full** — and on exactly the\nelement side A reaches. The split's `H`-branch runs `bside_branch` at `j = 0`\nand its `1`-branch at `j = 1`; that one index is the only difference between\nthem, and it is the extra `σ₀` the split leaves behind. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_resolves'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_resolves'","kind":"theorem","line":18304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18304-L18434","doc":"`bside_resolves`, carrying arbitrary surrounding terms.\n\nThe two hypotheses are exactly `bside_to_split'`'s. The branch steps need\nnothing further from the caller: their side conditions against the ambient\nterms follow from the head condition, and their side conditions against side\nB's *own* other term follow from a length count internal to this proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_branch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_branch","kind":"theorem","line":18264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18264-L18302","doc":"**One branch of side B's tail: two Bokut–Shiao steps.**\n\n`descWord i' 0 · descWord i j · σ_i ⟶* bsWord₂ i'' i' 0 · σ_i · descWord i' j`,\nfor either `j` — `j = 0` on the `H`-branch and `j = 1` on the `1`-branch, which\nis the only way the two differ. The trailing `σ_i` closes `descWord i j` into\n`bsWord₁ i j`; after that rule fires, `descWord i' 0` is closed by the\n`σ_{i'}` its `bsWord₂` put down, and the second rule fires on that.\n\nThe surrounding terms are arbitrary, subject only to a **length** condition:\nevery one of them must have a length other than this word's. All three words in\nthe chain have the same length — Bokut–Shiao is monic and length-preserving —\nso that single hypothesis discharges both steps' side conditions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_branch_core","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_branch_core","kind":"theorem","line":18228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18228-L18262","doc":"**One branch of side B's tail, with its two side conditions raw.**\n\n`bside_branch` derives both from a length hypothesis. That is the right\ndischarge inside side B, where every word of the chain has the same length,\nbut it is the wrong one at the joining: side A's normal form has exactly the\nlengths side B's post-split words do. Both words entering a step here open with\n`descWord i' 0`, so a *head* condition discharges them too — and a caller that\nneeds one shape for the ambient terms and the other for side B's own supplies\nwhichever it has. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₂_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₂_length","kind":"theorem","line":18222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18222-L18226","doc":"The Bokut–Shiao right-hand side is three letters longer than its\ndescending tail is deep. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_length'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_length'","kind":"theorem","line":18217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18217-L18220","doc":"Convenience form of `descWord_length`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_to_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_to_split","kind":"theorem","line":18203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18203-L18215","doc":"Side B, up to and including the split. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_to_split'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_to_split'","kind":"theorem","line":18153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18153-L18201","doc":"`bside_to_split`, carrying arbitrary surrounding terms.\n\n**Two hypotheses, of two different shapes, and the second is not optional.**\nThe sweep and the quadratic step both act with a fixed prefix in front, so a\nhead condition covers them. The *unshuffle* acts at the left end of the word —\n`a = []` — so nothing sits in front of it to separate on, and what protects it\nis the word's right end instead: no surrounding word may end in `σ₀σ₀σ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_length","kind":"theorem","line":18132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18132-L18151","doc":"**The length of a descending run.** `|descWord i j| = i − j + 1`. Proved on\nthe gap, like everything else about `descWord`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":18085,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18085-L18097","doc":"**Side A of the deep self-overlap resolves, in full.** One word, then the\nsingle quadratic step, landing on the two-term element\n`NF + (q − q⁻¹)·(NF · σ₀)` with `NF = bsWord₂ (i−2) (i−1) 0 · (descWord i 0).dropLast`.\nEverything before that step is monomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_resolves'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_resolves'","kind":"theorem","line":18054,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18054-L18083","doc":"`aside_resolves`, carrying arbitrary surrounding terms — **side A of `hdeep`\ninside an arbitrary S-polynomial**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_to_normalWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_to_normalWord","kind":"theorem","line":18039,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L18039-L18052","doc":"**Side A of the deep self-overlap, reduced to one word.**\n\nHead (§4bp) → unshuffle → one last carry: `σ_i` leaves the leading block and\ncrosses the lower run, which turns `σ_{i−2}σ_{i−1} ++ descWord (i−2) 0` into\n`bsWord₂ (i−2) (i−1) 0` and `σ_i ++ (descWord (i−1) 0).dropLast` into\n`(descWord i 0).dropLast`. What is left is a single word ending in `σ₀σ₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_to_normalWord'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_to_normalWord'","kind":"theorem","line":17975,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17975-L18037","doc":"`aside_to_normalWord`, carrying arbitrary surrounding terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairSweep_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairSweep_eq","kind":"theorem","line":17954,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17954-L17973","doc":"`pairSweep` is `pairList` with the trailing `σ_zσ_z` — the pairs, then the\none place the quadratic rule can fire. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairList_unshuffle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairList_unshuffle","kind":"theorem","line":17935,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17935-L17952","doc":"**The interleaved pairs unshuffle into two descending runs.**\n\n`pairList m z ⟶* descWord (m−1) z ++ (descWord m z).dropLast`, by one\n`gen_past_descWord` carry per level: the induction hypothesis separates the\npairs below, and then `σ_m` — the upper letter of the top pair — is carried\nrightward past the whole lower run it now sits in front of.\n\n`(descWord m z).dropLast` is the run with its bottom letter removed, which is\nthe upper run; writing it that way avoids naming `z + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairList_unshuffle'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairList_unshuffle'","kind":"theorem","line":17874,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17874-L17933","doc":"`pairList_unshuffle`, carrying arbitrary surrounding terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairList_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairList_cons","kind":"theorem","line":17866,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17866-L17872","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairList_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairList_self","kind":"theorem","line":17863,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17863-L17864","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairList","kind":"def","line":17857,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17857-L17861","doc":"`σ_{m−1}σ_m σ_{m−2}σ_{m−1} ⋯ σ_zσ_{z+1}` — `pairSweep` without its trailing\n`σ_zσ_z`, i.e. the interleaved pairs alone. Zipped against the run's own tail,\nso again no arithmetic on `Fin n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.gen_past_descWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.gen_past_descWord","kind":"theorem","line":17805,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17805-L17817","doc":"**A far generator commutes rightward past a whole descending run.**\n\n`σ_m · descWord k z ⟶* descWord k z · σ_m` whenever `k + 1 < m`, by one\nfar-commutation step per letter of the run. The induction is on the gap\n`k − z`, as `descWord_split_aux`'s is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.gen_past_descWord'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.gen_past_descWord'","kind":"theorem","line":17752,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17752-L17803","doc":"`gen_past_descWord`, carrying arbitrary surrounding terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_to_sweptWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_to_sweptWord","kind":"theorem","line":17710,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17710-L17720","doc":"**Side A of the deep self-overlap, swept.** The three-step head lands on a\ndoubled descending run, and §4bo's sweep takes it from there — so side A costs\n`3 + (i − 1)` steps to here, not the `(i²+i+4)/2` the greedy reduction spends\nreaching its own split word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_to_sweptWord'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_to_sweptWord'","kind":"theorem","line":17689,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17689-L17708","doc":"`aside_to_sweptWord`, carrying arbitrary surrounding terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_head","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_head","kind":"theorem","line":17679,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17679-L17687","doc":"**Side A's opening: three steps to a doubled descending run.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_head'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.aside_head'","kind":"theorem","line":17600,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17600-L17677","doc":"`aside_head`, carrying arbitrary surrounding terms.\n\nIts three steps sit in three different contexts, but each word begins with\n`σ_i` or `σ_{i−2}` — so two head conditions, `CtxAvoids L [σ_x] []` saying no\nsurrounding word begins with `σ_x`, cover all of them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_to_splitWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_to_splitWord","kind":"theorem","line":17554,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17554-L17571","doc":"**Side B of the deep self-overlap reaches its split word.**\n\n`B = bsWord₂ i' i 0 ++ descWord i' 0 ++ [σᵢ]` is `σ_{i−1}σ_i` in front of a\ndoubled descending run, so the sweep applies verbatim in that context and lands\non `pairSweep i 0 ++ [σᵢ]` — the word `σ_{i−1}σ_i σ_{i−2}σ_{i−1} ⋯ σ₀σ₁ σ₀σ₀ σᵢ`\nwhose single `σ₀σ₀` is where the one quadratic step of the whole reduction\nhappens. `i − 1` steps, one per level.\n\nThis is the `hdeep` obligation's B-half up to the split; the A-half is a\ndifferent and doubly-nested chain, and is not this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_to_splitWord'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bside_to_splitWord'","kind":"theorem","line":17524,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17524-L17552","doc":"`bside_to_splitWord`, carrying arbitrary surrounding terms.\n\nEvery word of the sweep sits behind the fixed prefix `σ_{i−1}σ_i`, so the\nsingle head condition \"no surrounding word begins with `σ_{i−1}`\" covers the\nwhole run. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.doubleDesc_sweep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.doubleDesc_sweep","kind":"theorem","line":17504,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17504-L17522","doc":"**A doubled descending run sweeps to interleaved pairs.**\n\n`descWord m z ++ descWord m z ⟶* pairSweep m z`, by exactly one Bokut–Shiao\nstep per level: the second copy's head `σ_m` closes the first copy into\n`bsWord₁ m z`, the rule replaces it by `bsWord₂ (m−1) m z = σ_{m−1}σ_m ++\ndescWord (m−1) z`, and what is left is the same shape one level down. The\nbottom level needs no step at all — `descWord z z ++ descWord z z` *is*\n`σ_z σ_z`.\n\nStated on a one-term element, so `monicStep`'s side condition on the\nsurrounding terms is vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.doubleDesc_sweep'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.doubleDesc_sweep'","kind":"theorem","line":17457,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17457-L17502","doc":"`doubleDesc_sweep`, carrying arbitrary surrounding terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.mem_ctx_or_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.mem_ctx_or_eq","kind":"theorem","line":17447,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17447-L17455","doc":"Membership in a context with one distinguished extra term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CtxAvoids.ne_descWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CtxAvoids.ne_descWord","kind":"theorem","line":17435,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17435-L17445","doc":"A word that *opens* with a descending run is avoided by a context that\navoids that run's head letter. This is the workhorse turning a head condition\ninto the plain `≠` a step lemma asks for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ctxAvoids_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ctxAvoids_nil","kind":"theorem","line":17430,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17430-L17433","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CtxAvoids.ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CtxAvoids.ne","kind":"theorem","line":17422,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17422-L17428","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CtxAvoids.narrow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CtxAvoids.narrow","kind":"theorem","line":17416,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17416-L17420","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CtxAvoids.extendRight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CtxAvoids.extendRight","kind":"theorem","line":17410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17410-L17414","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CtxAvoids.extend","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CtxAvoids.extend","kind":"theorem","line":17404,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17404-L17408","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CtxAvoids","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CtxAvoids","kind":"def","line":17397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17397-L17402","doc":"The context condition the whole joining threads: every surrounding term\ndiffers from **every** word of the shape `a ++ _ ++ b`. Every intermediate of a\nchain that rewrites strictly inside `a … b` has that shape, so this one\nhypothesis discharges all of their side conditions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairSweep_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairSweep_self","kind":"theorem","line":17361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17361-L17364","doc":"At the bottom the sweep is already done. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairSweep_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairSweep_cons","kind":"theorem","line":17352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17352-L17359","doc":"The recursion the sweep runs on: one pair peels off the front. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairSweep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.pairSweep","kind":"def","line":17345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17345-L17350","doc":"`σ_{m−1}σ_m σ_{m−2}σ_{m−1} ⋯ σ_{z}σ_{z+1} σ_z σ_z` — the word a doubled\ndescending run sweeps to. Defined by zipping the run against its own tail so\nthat no arithmetic on `Fin n` is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompleted_isGrobnerShirshovBasis_of_deep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompleted_isGrobnerShirshovBasis_of_deep","kind":"theorem","line":17290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17290-L17307","doc":"**The completed Hecke rewriting system is a Gröbner–Shirshov basis**, modulo\nthe single deep-diagonal self-overlap.\n\n`hdeep` is discharged in §4bw by `deep_selfOverlap_resolves`, and\n`heckeCompleted_isGrobnerShirshovBasis` at the end of this file is the\nunconditional statement. This form is kept because the two halves are proved\nfar apart: everything above depends only on the conditional one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlap_resolves_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlap_resolves_general","kind":"theorem","line":17231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17231-L17252","doc":"**Every overlap composition of the completed Hecke system resolves**, modulo\nthe one deep-diagonal self-overlap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiao_right_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiao_right_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":17175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17175-L17229","doc":"**The `? × BS` column of `overlap_resolves`**, modulo the deep diagonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yangBaxter_right_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yangBaxter_right_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":17137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17137-L17173","doc":"**The `? × YB` column of `overlap_resolves`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlap_letter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlap_letter","kind":"theorem","line":17118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17118-L17135","doc":"The overlap letter, read off both leading monomials at once. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlap_resolves_of_nil_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlap_resolves_of_nil_left","kind":"theorem","line":17077,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17077-L17085","doc":"…so it resolves, in no reduction steps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlap_spoly_isZero_of_nil_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlap_spoly_isZero_of_nil_left","kind":"theorem","line":17053,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L17053-L17075","doc":"**A nil-left overlap composition has zero S-polynomial** — no reduction\nneeded, for any two rules of the completed system. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_right_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_right_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":16978,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16978-L17031","doc":"**The `? × FC` row of `overlap_resolves`, for an arbitrary composition.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yb_farComm_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yb_farComm_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":16947,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16947-L16976","doc":"**Yang–Baxter against far commutation**, for an arbitrary composition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_left_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_left_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":16869,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16869-L16926","doc":"**The `FC × ?` row of `overlap_resolves`, for an arbitrary composition.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_farComm_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_farComm_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":16836,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16836-L16867","doc":"**Far commutation against far commutation** — the member §4q never\ninstantiated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bs_farComm_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bs_farComm_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":16734,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16734-L16810","doc":"**Bokut–Shiao against far commutation, for an arbitrary composition.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.braid_bs_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.braid_bs_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":16668,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16668-L16705","doc":"**A rule on the braid word against Bokut–Shiao** — the mirror. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bs_braid_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bs_braid_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":16625,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16625-L16666","doc":"**Bokut–Shiao against a rule on the braid word, for an arbitrary\ncomposition.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.braid_self_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.braid_self_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":16573,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16573-L16605","doc":"**The braid-word cell of `overlap_resolves`, for an arbitrary composition.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_eq_wHi_cases","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_eq_wHi_cases","kind":"theorem","line":16543,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16543-L16571","doc":"**Only two rules lead on the braid word.** No hypothesis relating `i'` to\n`i` is needed: matching a leading monomial against `[σᵢ, σᵢ', σᵢ]` *forces*\n`i' + 1 = i` in both surviving families, so the side condition is an output\nrather than an input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quad_left_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quad_left_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":16402,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16402-L16483","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quad_right_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quad_right_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":16301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16301-L16380","doc":"**The `? × quadratic` column of `overlap_resolves`, for an arbitrary\ncomposition.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.oc_ext_of_left_ne_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.oc_ext_of_left_ne_nil","kind":"theorem","line":16255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16255-L16299","doc":"**An overlap composition with a non-empty left context is determined by its\ntwo rules.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.inclusion_resolves_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.inclusion_resolves_general","kind":"theorem","line":16208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16208-L16226","doc":"**The inclusion half of the Gröbner–Shirshov condition, for every `n`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.shared_lm_classify","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.shared_lm_classify","kind":"theorem","line":16106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16106-L16206","doc":"**Two rules sharing a leading monomial are the same rule, or §4j's pair.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_eq_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_eq_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":16092,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16092-L16104","doc":"A descending run of length one is the singleton at its own top. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₁_length_ge_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₁_length_ge_three","kind":"theorem","line":16084,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16084-L16090","doc":"A Bokut–Shiao word has length at least three: `bsWord₁_cons` exposes two\nletters, and the descending run between them is itself non-empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.inclusion_contexts_empty_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.inclusion_contexts_empty_general","kind":"theorem","line":16037,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16037-L16050","doc":"**Every inclusion composition of the completed system has empty contexts, for\nevery `n`.** §4m proves this at `n = 4` off a `decide`d antichain; with\n`lm_infix_antichain` the same argument runs at every `n`, and needs no hypothesis\nabout which rules are involved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_infix_antichain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_infix_antichain","kind":"theorem","line":16019,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L16019-L16035","doc":"**The leading monomials of the completed system form an infix antichain, for\nevery `n`.** §4m's `completedLMSet_four_infix_antichain` decides this at `n = 4`;\nthis is the same statement proved, and it is the three cases above assembled. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_not_proper_interior","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_not_proper_interior","kind":"theorem","line":15964,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15964-L16017","doc":"**A leading monomial is not strictly interior to another.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.repeat_of_head_eq_last","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.repeat_of_head_eq_last","kind":"theorem","line":15950,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15950-L15961","doc":"Inside a duplicate-free run, a word cannot repeat its own head as its last\nletter: `nodup_split_unique` reads the head's position two ways. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":15911,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15911-L15948","doc":"**Adjacent letters of a descending run drop by exactly one.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.nodup_split_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.nodup_split_unique","kind":"theorem","line":15884,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15884-L15909","doc":"**In a duplicate-free list, a letter pins its own position.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_last","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_last","kind":"theorem","line":15873,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15873-L15882","doc":"**The descending run ends on its bottom letter.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":15866,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15866-L15871","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_not_proper_prefix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_not_proper_prefix","kind":"theorem","line":15775,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15775-L15832","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_not_proper_suffix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_not_proper_suffix","kind":"theorem","line":15708,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15708-L15748","doc":"**No leading monomial of the completed system is a proper suffix of\nanother.** Half of §4m's `n = 4` antichain, for every `n`.\n\nIf `lm₂ = left ++ lm₁` with `left` non-empty, then `lm₁`'s head lands in `lm₂`'s\n*interior*, so it is strictly below `lm₂`'s head. But `lm₁`'s last letter is\n`lm₂`'s last letter, and — unless `lm₂` is the two-letter far-commutation word,\nwhose interior is empty and so cannot contain anything — that equals `lm₂`'s\nhead. Since a head dominates its own word, `lm₂`'s head is at most `lm₁`'s head,\nwhich is strictly below it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_cons_snoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_cons_snoc","kind":"theorem","line":15693,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15693-L15706","doc":"**Every leading monomial has a head, an interior and a last letter** — i.e.\nhas length at least two. Bokut–Shiao is the only family where that needs an\nargument, and `descWord_cons` supplies it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_last_eq_head_or_far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_last_eq_head_or_far","kind":"theorem","line":15675,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15675-L15691","doc":"**A leading monomial's last letter either matches its head, or drops by more\nthan one.** Two–one split across the four families: quadratic, Yang–Baxter and\nBokut–Shiao all end on their own top letter; far-commutation is the exception,\nand its drop is at least two by its own side condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_interior_lt_head","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_interior_lt_head","kind":"theorem","line":15651,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15651-L15673","doc":"**The interior of a leading monomial is strictly below its head.** The\nquadratic and far-commutation words have no interior at all; Yang–Baxter's is the\nsingle letter `σᵢ` below its head `σᵢ₊₁`; and Bokut–Shiao's is the descending run\n`descWord i' j`, capped at `i − 1` by `descWord_index_le`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_split","kind":"theorem","line":15610,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15610-L15649","doc":"**A leading monomial, split into head, interior and last letter.**\nEvery branch has the shape `mid ++ [l] = <explicit interior> ++ [<explicit\nlast>]`, so one `List.append_inj'` reads off both at once. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsbs_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsbs_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":15557,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15557-L15570","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsbs_resolves_of_nil_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsbs_resolves_of_nil_left","kind":"theorem","line":15493,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15493-L15555","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_bot_inj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_bot_inj","kind":"theorem","line":15486,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15486-L15491","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_bot_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_bot_mem","kind":"theorem","line":15480,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15480-L15484","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsbs_resolves_of_oc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsbs_resolves_of_oc","kind":"theorem","line":15424,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15424-L15448","doc":"**The criterion's obligation for an arbitrary Bokut–Shiao × Bokut–Shiao\ncomposition.** `bsbs_overlap_resolves` speaks about the *constructed*\n`CornerGeneral.oc`; `IsGrobnerShirshovBasis.overlap_resolves` quantifies over\nevery `OverlapComposition`. `bsbs_oc_eq` closes that gap, and `bsbs_top_eq`\nmeans the two rules need not be assumed to share a top — a one-letter overlap\nforces it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsbs_top_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsbs_top_eq","kind":"theorem","line":15389,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15389-L15422","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsbs_oc_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsbs_oc_eq","kind":"theorem","line":15349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15349-L15387","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlap_length_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlap_length_one","kind":"theorem","line":15252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15252-L15315","doc":"**Every composition with a non-empty left context overlaps in one letter.**\nThe general statement, over all four rule shapes, of what\n`hecke_overlap_length_probe.py` measures at `n ≤ 8`.\n\nThree of the four are a length bound rather than an argument: the quadratic and\nfar-commutation leading monomials have length 2, so one letter of left context\nalready leaves exactly one; Yang–Baxter has length 3, and its one escape — a\ntwo-letter overlap `[σᵢ, σⱼ]` — puts `σⱼ` behind `σᵢ` at the head of `lm₂`,\nwhich `lm_head_is_max` forbids since `j = i + 1`. Only the Bokut–Shiao case\nneeds `overlap_length_one_of_bs_left`.\n\nNote the hypothesis is `oc.left ≠ []` **alone**. The probe measures the\n*proper* compositions, where the right context is non-empty too; the Lean does\nnot need that, so this covers `left ≠ [] , right = []` as well. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlap_length_one_of_bs_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlap_length_one_of_bs_left","kind":"theorem","line":15195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15195-L15250","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_head_is_max","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.lm_head_is_max","kind":"theorem","line":15153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15153-L15193","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerCriterion.bsbs_overlap_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerCriterion.bsbs_overlap_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":15020,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15020-L15093","doc":"**Every Bokut–Shiao × Bokut–Shiao overlap at top `i − 1` resolves.**\n\nThe case analysis is on the two depths, and it is the only new content:\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `j₁ < j₂` | `sPoly_gt_resolves` — the `a > b` corner, uniform in `a` |\n| `j₂ ≤ j₁`, `j₁ = i₁` | `sPoly_le_resolves₁` |\n| `j₂ ≤ j₁`, `j₁ + 1 = i₁` | `sPoly_le_resolves₂` |\n| `j₂ ≤ j₁`, `j₁ + 2 = i₁` | `sPoly_le_resolves₃` |\n| `j₂ ≤ j₁`, `j₁ + 3 ≤ i₁` | `sPoly_le_resolves` |\n\n`jm` is `j₁ − 1`, and it does not always exist. Only the `a ≥ 2` branches need\nit — the `a = 1` branch and the whole `a > b` regime never mention it — so it is\n**derived inside the proof**, from `hcov`, rather than taken as a parameter. As a\nparameter it blocked `j₁ = 0` outright, including the cases whose reduction\nchains already exist.\n\n`hcov : 1 ≤ j₁ ∨ 1 ≤ j₂ ∨ i₁ = 0` is exactly the complement of the gap: its\nnegation is `j₁ = 0 ∧ j₂ = 0 ∧ i₁ ≥ 1`. Each disjunct discharges the `a ≥ 2`\nbranch differently — the first directly; the second because `j₂ ≤ j₁` holds\nthere, so `1 ≤ j₂` gives `1 ≤ j₁`; the third **vacuously**, since that branch\nalso carries `j₁ + 1 ≤ i₁`, which `i₁ = 0` contradicts.\n\nSo what remains open is the deep diagonal `j₁ = j₂ = 0` **with `i₁ ≥ 1`** — not\nall of `j₁ = 0`, as this section previously said. `j₁ = 0` with `j₂ ≥ 1` is the\n`a > b` regime and was always covered; `j₁ = j₂ = i₁ = 0` is the `a = 1` branch\nand was too. That is a real gap, not a stylistic one, and the hypothesis is now\nstated so that its negation names the gap exactly.\n\n`hq` is needed only by the `a = 1` branch, where the first term carries\ncoefficient `h` and a `SingleStepReduction` needs it nonzero to transport. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerCriterion.resolves_of_T0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerCriterion.resolves_of_T0","kind":"theorem","line":15000,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L15000-L15018","doc":"**From a `T0` chain to the criterion's obligation.** Every corner theorem\nends `∃ E, T0 →* E ∧ CoeffEq E 0`; this is that, restated for `oc.spoly`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPoly_gt_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPoly_gt_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":14955,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14955-L14973","doc":"**The `a > b` corner is closed.** The S-polynomial of the two Bokut–Shiao\nrules at top `i − 1` with bottoms `j₁ < j₂ ≤ i − 1` reduces to an element that\nis zero. Both halves are needed and neither is decoration: the reduction says\nthe completion procedure *reaches* the element, and the coefficient equality\nsays nothing is left when it gets there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPolyChain_gt_all","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPolyChain_gt_all","kind":"theorem","line":14930,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14930-L14953","doc":"**The `a > b` corner, for every `a > b ≥ 1`.**\n\n`hb : j₂ ≤ i₁` is `b ≥ 1`; `hj₁ : j₁ ≤ j₂ − 1` is `a > b`. Nothing else is\nassumed — in particular nothing about `a`, which is the measured\n`a`-independence of this corner.\n\nThe case split is on `b`, not on `a`: `sPolyChain_gt` for `b ≥ 2`, and\n`sPolyChain_gt₁` for `b = 1`, where `j₂ > i₂` forces `j₂ = i₁` and the first\nlineage's run is empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.WGt₁_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.WGt₁_eq","kind":"theorem","line":14922,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14922-L14928","doc":"**`WGt₁` is `WGt` at `b = 1`.** At `j₂ = i₁` the predecessor `j₂'` is `i₂`,\nand `descWord i₂ i₂` is a single letter, so `bsWord₂ i₂ i₁ i₂` is exactly the\nthree letters `WGt₁` writes out. The two lineages meet at the same word in\nboth regimes; only its shape differs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPoly_zero_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPoly_zero_gt","kind":"theorem","line":14911,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14911-L14918","doc":"**The `a > b` S-polynomial resolves to zero at every `b ≥ 2`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPolyChain_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPolyChain_gt","kind":"theorem","line":14762,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14762-L14909","doc":"**The `a > b` chain at every `b ≥ 2`**, `T0` to a two-term element whose\nentries are equal and oppositely signed.\n\n`hb : j₂ ≤ i₂` is `b ≥ 2`; `hj₁ : j₁ ≤ j₂ − 1` is `a > b`, the corner's own\nhypothesis, and it is what gives the last block of each run its floor room.\nNothing constrains `a` beyond that, which is the measured `a`-independence of\nthis corner.\n\nAt `b = 2` this is `sPolyChain_gt₂`, proved separately first: `gtRun` was\nwritten *after* that concrete case, so that the induction step was designed\nagainst words that had already been checked against the engine. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.WGt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.WGt","kind":"def","line":14755,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14755-L14759","doc":"The word both lineages reach, at any `b`: `bsWord₂ i₂ i₁ (j₂ − 1)` followed\nby `descWord i j₁`, with `j₂'` standing for `j₂ − 1`. `WGt₁` and `WGt₂` are its\n`b = 1` and `b = 2` shapes written out. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPoly_zero_gt₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPoly_zero_gt₂","kind":"theorem","line":14732,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14732-L14741","doc":"**The `a > b` S-polynomial resolves to zero at `b = 2`.** Same cancellation\nas at `b = 1`: the two entries are the same word with opposite signs and are\nadjacent, so nothing survives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPolyChain_gt₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPolyChain_gt₂","kind":"theorem","line":14533,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14533-L14730","doc":"**The whole `a > b` chain at `b = 2`**, fifteen steps, `T0` to a two-term\nelement whose entries are equal and oppositely signed.\n\nEight steps on the first term (`vOpen`'s five, then one block's three), seven on\nthe second (two blocks of two and three, then the two closing Bokut–Shiao\nsteps). As at `b = 1` there is **no quadratic step**, so neither term splits and\nthe `1` / `−1` they start with survive to the meeting.\n\nEvery collision hypothesis is a **head**: the first lineage's words open `σᵢ` or\n`σᵢ₋₂`, the second's open `σᵢ₋₁`, and the word the first parks on opens\n`σᵢ₋₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.U0_eq_gt₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.U0_eq_gt₂","kind":"theorem","line":14516,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14516-L14524","doc":"**`U0` at `b = 2`.** `descWord i₁ j₂` is the two letters `σᵢ₋₁ σᵢ₋₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.V0_eq_gt₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.V0_eq_gt₂","kind":"theorem","line":14503,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14503-L14514","doc":"**`V0` at `b = 2`.** `descWord i j₂` is `[σᵢ, σᵢ₋₁, σᵢ₋₂]`, so the term is\n`vOpen`'s source with the one-letter trailing context `S = [σᵢ₋₂]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.WGt₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.WGt₂","kind":"def","line":14497,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14497-L14501","doc":"The word both lineages reach at `b = 2`. This is\n`bsWord₂ i₂ i₁ (j₂ − 1) ++ descWord i j₁` at `j₂ = i₂`, where `j₂ − 1` is `i₃`\nand `descWord i₂ i₃` is the two letters `σᵢ₋₂ σᵢ₋₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPoly_zero_gt₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPoly_zero_gt₁","kind":"theorem","line":14461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14461-L14476","doc":"**The `a > b` S-polynomial resolves to zero at `b = 1`.** The two entries\n`sPolyChain_gt₁` lands on are the same word with opposite signs, so they\ncontribute nothing and the element is zero.\n\nThey are **adjacent**, which is why this is `ofTerms_cancel_pair` and not\n`CornerLe`'s `ofTerms_cancel_split`: there, `trio`'s quadratic step emits each\nlineage's `h`-weighted word immediately before its plain one, so the two\ncancelling entries are separated by two survivors. Here nothing splits, so\nnothing sits between them — and nothing survives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPolyChain_gt₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.sPolyChain_gt₁","kind":"theorem","line":14320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14320-L14459","doc":"**The whole `a > b` chain at `b = 1`**, nine steps, `T0` to a two-term\nelement whose entries are equal and oppositely signed.\n\nFive steps on the first term, four on the second. Every step is a `bsStep` or a\none-letter far-commutation `σᵢ σᵢ₋₂ → σᵢ₋₂ σᵢ`; there is **no quadratic step**,\nso neither term ever splits and no coefficient moves — the two terms keep the\n`1` and `−1` they start with, which is what makes the meeting a cancellation.\n\nThe fourth step of the second lineage is `bokutShiaoRelation i₂ i₁ i₂`, whose\nbottom equals the pair's lower index. That is the rule the engine's trace names\n`Y`: it shares a leading word with Yang–Baxter and differs by a sign, so the\nmonic Bokut–Shiao form is the one that applies — §4al makes the same move one\nlevel down for `quadPair`.\n\nEvery collision hypothesis is a **head**. The first lineage's words open `σᵢ`\nor `σᵢ₋₂` and the second's open `σᵢ₋₁`; once the first has finished, the word\nit parks on opens `σᵢ₋₂`, still against `σᵢ₋₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.WGt₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.WGt₁","kind":"def","line":14306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14306-L14310","doc":"The word both lineages reach, where the element vanishes. This is\n`bsWord₂ i₂ i₁ (j₂ − 1) ++ descWord i j₁` at `j₂ = i₁`, where `j₂ − 1` is `i₂`\nand `descWord i₂ i₂` is a single letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.vOpen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.vOpen","kind":"theorem","line":14174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14174-L14304","doc":"**The first lineage's opening, for any `b`.** Five steps, from\n`descWord i j₁ ++ ([σᵢ₋₁, σᵢ, σᵢ₋₁] ++ S)` to\n`[σᵢ₋₂, σᵢ₋₁, σᵢ₋₂] ++ (descWord i j₁ ++ S)`, with `S` an arbitrary trailing\ncontext carried inert throughout.\n\n`S` is what makes this `b`-independent. The S-polynomial's first term is\n`descWord i j₁ ++ (σᵢ₋₁ :: descWord i j₂)`, and `descWord i j₂` splits as\n`[σᵢ, σᵢ₋₁] ++ descWord i₂ j₂`; the second factor never participates, so\n`S = descWord i₂ j₂` and `b = 1` is the case `S = []`.\n`hecke_agtb_lineage_schedule.py` measures that 10/10 — the words at every\n`b ≥ 2` are the `b = 1` words with exactly that suffix appended. (Its one\nexception, `a = 3, b = 2`, is a genuine index coincidence at the *fifth* step,\nrecorded there; this lemma is stated for the general case and simply does not\napply to it.)\n\n**Two hypotheses cover all five collisions**, because the words this run\ntouches open only two letters: `σᵢ` for the first two and `σᵢ₋₂` for the last\nthree. Neither mentions `S`, which is why the generalisation costs nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.U0_eq_gt₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.U0_eq_gt₁","kind":"theorem","line":14162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14162-L14169","doc":"**`U0` at `b = 1`.** Same collapse on the other term: `descWord i₁ j₂` is\nthe single letter `σᵢ₋₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.V0_eq_gt₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.V0_eq_gt₁","kind":"theorem","line":14152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14152-L14160","doc":"**`V0` at `b = 1`.** `descWord i j₂` is `[σᵢ, σᵢ₋₁]`, so the term ends in\nthree letters rather than a run. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.gtRun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.gtRun","kind":"theorem","line":14020,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L14020-L14144","doc":"**The whole run, at any length** — `gtBlock` iterated.\n\nEach block pulls the **leading letter** of the trailing descending run across\n`descWord i j₁`, demotes it by one, and deposits it on the left. So the run\n`descWord y j₂` slides down by one — to `descWord z j₂'` — and jumps to the\nleft of `descWord i j₁`. `k` is the number of blocks minus one: the run has\n`k + 1` letters.\n\n`z` and `j₂'` are the predecessors of `y` and `j₂`, passed as parameters with\n`+ 1 =` hypotheses rather than constructed. That is this file's idiom for a\n`Fin n` predecessor (`descWord_cons_le` takes its `i'` the same way), and it is\nwhat keeps the induction free of `Fin n` arithmetic: the one place a\npredecessor must be *built* is the recursive call's `z − 1`.\n\n`hsplit : w ++ descWord y j₁ = descWord i j₁` is what makes the block\napplicable — the redex `bsWord₁ y j₁` is the tail of `descWord i j₁` from `y`\ndown, plus the run's leading letter. Carrying it as a hypothesis means no `Fin\nn` **successor** is ever needed for `w`, which is what a direct\n`w = descWord i (y+1)` would have forced.\n\n`hj₁ : j₁ ≤ j₂'` is the corner's own hypothesis `a > b` — the last block, which\nconsumes `σⱼ₂`, needs floor room one below `j₂`.\n\n**Both lineages are this one lemma.** The first at `a₀ = σᵢ₋₂`,\n`A₀ = [σᵢ₋₁, σᵢ₋₂]`, `w = descWord i i₁`, `y = i₂`, `B = []`; the second at\n`a₀ = σᵢ₋₁`, `A₀ = []`, `w = [σᵢ]`, `y = i₁`, `B = [σᵢ]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.gtBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGt.gtBlock","kind":"theorem","line":13983,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13983-L14018","doc":"**One block.** `bsStep` at `(x, x+1, j₁)`, then the `σₓ` it emits transports\nleft past `w`.\n\nThe two compose with nothing between them because `bsWord₂ x x' j₁` *opens*\nwith `σₓ`: the Bokut–Shiao step's output is the transport's input on the nose,\nwith the run `w` sitting in the step's own left context. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.sPoly_le_resolves₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.sPoly_le_resolves₁","kind":"theorem","line":13880,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13880-L13936","doc":"**The `a = 1` S-polynomial resolves.** The six entries the tail lands on\nannihilate in three pairs — two split, one adjacent — so the element is zero.\n\nThe join is the one #5586 built: `prefixChain₁` to `TCancel₁`,\n`TCancel₁_coeffEq` to drop the cancelling pair it already carries, then the\ntail, absorbed through `MultiStepReduction.congr_source`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailFromCancel₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailFromCancel₁","kind":"theorem","line":13723,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13723-L13878","doc":"**The `a = 1` tail** — `tailPair₁` straight to zero.\n\nTwo separation arguments are needed, not one. The first and fourth terms both\nopen `σᵢ₋₁`, so a head does not tell them apart from the transports'\nintermediates; **length** does, and that is what `hlen` is for. The second and\nthird terms open `σᵢ` and are separated by a head throughout. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailPair₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailPair₁","kind":"def","line":13713,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13713-L13720","doc":"The four words `TCancel₁_coeffEq` leaves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.sPoly_le_resolves₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.sPoly_le_resolves₂","kind":"theorem","line":13661,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13661-L13689","doc":"**The `a = 2` S-polynomial resolves.** Same join as `sPoly_le_resolves`:\n`prefixChain₂` to `TCancel₂`, `TCancel₂_coeffEq` to drop the cancelling `WStar`\npair, then the tail to a sign-pair, absorbed through\n`MultiStepReduction.congr_source`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailFromCancel₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailFromCancel₂","kind":"theorem","line":13503,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13503-L13659","doc":"**The `a = 2` tail** — `tailPair₂` to a sign-pair at `tailMeet₂`.\n\nEvery collision hypothesis is a **head**: the first lineage's words open `σᵢ₋₂`\nthroughout and the second's open `σᵢ₋₁`, and the word the first parks on opens\n`σᵢ₋₂`. No length or letter-position argument is needed, unlike the `a ≥ 3`\nprefix, whose three bystanders needed three different separation shapes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailPair₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailPair₂","kind":"def","line":13492,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13492-L13497","doc":"The two words `TCancel₂_coeffEq` leaves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailMeet₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailMeet₂","kind":"def","line":13488,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13488-L13490","doc":"The word the two `a = 2` tail lineages meet at. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.sPoly_le_resolves₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.sPoly_le_resolves₃","kind":"theorem","line":13435,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13435-L13467","doc":"**The same, at `a = 3`** — `prefixChain₃` lands on the same `TCancel`, so the\ntail and the join are unchanged and only the prefix differs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.sPoly_le_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.sPoly_le_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":13388,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13388-L13433","doc":"**The `a ≤ b` S-polynomial resolves, for every `a ≥ 3`.**\n\n`prefixChain` reaches `TCancel`, `TCancel_coeffEq` drops its cancelling `WStar`\npair, `tailFromCancel` runs the tail to a sign-pair, and that pair is zero.\n\nThe `CoeffEq` in the middle is why this needs `congr_source` rather than a\n`trans`: `TCancel` and `tailPair` are the same element but not the same\n*representation*, and `MultiStepReduction` is stated on representations. The\ndisjunction `congr_source` returns costs nothing — in the left branch the chain\nruns on from `TCancel`, in the right branch `TCancel` was already the endpoint,\nand either way the element is coefficientwise zero.\n\n`a = 3` is included: `prefixChain₃` lands on the same `TCancel`, so\n`sPolyResolves_le₃` differs only in which prefix it composes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailFromCancel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailFromCancel","kind":"theorem","line":13361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13361-L13386","doc":"**The tail, for every `b`** — `tailPair` to the sign-pair at `tailMeet`.\n\nThe case split is on the diagonal, not on `a`: `tailChain` runs off it and\n`tailChainFromTwo` on it. Their **targets** are literally the same expression, so\nonly the sources need reconciling, and the two lemmas above do that. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailPair_eq_fromTwo_source","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailPair_eq_fromTwo_source","kind":"theorem","line":13334,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13334-L13359","doc":"**`tailPair` is `tailChainFromTwo`'s source on the diagonal.**\n\nAt `j₂ = j₁` the two sources coincide, and only there: `descWord jm j₂` is\n**empty** (`jm < j₁ = j₂`) while `descWord j₁ j₂` is the single letter `σ_j₁`, so\n`tailChainFromTwo`'s trailing `σ_jp` — which sits *after* its `descWord j₁ j₂`\nrather than before — lands in the same place as `tailPair`'s. Off the diagonal\nthe two words genuinely differ, which is why neither tail statement subsumes the\nother. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailPair_eq_tailChain_source","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailPair_eq_tailChain_source","kind":"theorem","line":13314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13314-L13332","doc":"**`tailPair` is `tailChain`'s source**, off the diagonal.\n\nOne `descWord_cons_le` does it, and it is applied to **both** entries at once\nrather than to the second alone: `trioLeft i i₁ i₂` opens `σᵢ₋₁` where\n`tailChain`'s second term opens `descWord i₁ jpp`, and peeling that everywhere\nputs the two in the same shape without disturbing the first entry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailMeet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailMeet","kind":"def","line":13309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13309-L13312","doc":"The word both tail lineages meet at. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.tailPair","kind":"def","line":13299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13299-L13307","doc":"The two words `TCancel_coeffEq` leaves — `TCancel` with its cancelling\n`WStar` pair removed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.uHead","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.uHead","kind":"theorem","line":13278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13278-L13286","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TCancel₁_coeffEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TCancel₁_coeffEq","kind":"theorem","line":13249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13249-L13276","doc":"**The `a = 1` cancellation.** Same shape as `TCancel_coeffEq` and\n`TCancel₂_coeffEq`: the two `bsWord₂ i₁ i j₂` entries carry `h²` and `−h²` and\nare not adjacent, so this is `ofTerms_cancel_split`. What survives is the two\nplain V words and the two plain U words. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.prefixChain₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.prefixChain₁","kind":"theorem","line":13142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13142-L13247","doc":"**The whole `a = 1` prefix**, six steps: a quadratic step on each term,\nthen the U lineage's `bsStep` and its second quadratic step, then the V\nlineage's braid step and its second quadratic step. The two `h²`-weighted\ncopies of `bsWord₂ i₁ i j₂` are what cancel.\n\nThe V lineage's braid step is `bsStep` at `j = i₁` — the degenerate\nBokut–Shiao rule that shares a leading word with Yang–Baxter — and on the\ndiagonal `b = 1` so is the U lineage's. The engine's trace names both `Y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TCancel₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TCancel₁","kind":"def","line":13134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13134-L13140","doc":"The `a = 1` chain at its first cancellation: `bsWord₂ i₁ i j₂` twice, with\n`h²` and `−h²`, separated by the two plain V words. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.U0_eq₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.U0_eq₁","kind":"theorem","line":13121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13121-L13132","doc":"**`U0` at `a = 1`.** The same collapse on the other term: `descWord i₁ j₂`\nopens `σᵢ₋₁`, and it meets the `σᵢ₋₁` ending `descWord i j₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.V0_eq₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.V0_eq₁","kind":"theorem","line":13104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13104-L13119","doc":"**`V0` at `a = 1`.** Two descending runs collapse: `descWord i j₁` is\n`[σᵢ, σᵢ₋₁]`, and the `σᵢ₋₁` the S-polynomial inserts lands against the second\nof them — that adjacency is the quadratic redex. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TCancel₂_coeffEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TCancel₂_coeffEq","kind":"theorem","line":13065,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13065-L13079","doc":"**The `a = 2` cancellation.** Same shape as `TCancel_coeffEq`: the two\n`WStar` entries carry `h` and `−h` and are not adjacent, so this is\n`ofTerms_cancel_split`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.prefixChain₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.prefixChain₂","kind":"theorem","line":13054,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13054-L13063","doc":"**The whole `a = 2` prefix**, `a² + a + 5 = 11` steps — the same count\nformula as `a ≥ 3`, and the same `WStar` cancellation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingPhase₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingPhase₂","kind":"theorem","line":13041,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L13041-L13052","doc":"**The `a = 2` closing phase, whole** — `4(a − 1) = 4` steps, `TOpen₂` to the\ncancellation. The same three calls as `a ≥ 3` (`fRun`, `closingBs`, `fRun`),\nwith both F-runs one step because the run is empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingV₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingV₂","kind":"theorem","line":12968,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12968-L13039","doc":"**The `a = 2` V lineage's closing run**: one `fRun_gen`, again over an empty\nrun, landing on the very word the U lineage just reached. No `closingBs` — the V\nlineage's two `bsStep`s were spent in its trio.\n\n`WStar` opens `σᵢ₋₂ σᵢ₋₁` exactly as this run's source does, so the bystander\nargument here is the **third** letter: the source's is `σᵢ`, `WStar`'s is\n`σ_j₁`, and `j₁ = i₂` is two below `i`. Length does not separate them — both are\n`|descWord jm j₂| + 6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TCancel₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TCancel₂","kind":"def","line":12958,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12958-L12966","doc":"The `a = 2` chain at its first cancellation: `WStar` twice, with `h` and\n`−h`, separated by the plain V word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingU₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingU₂","kind":"theorem","line":12841,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12841-L12956","doc":"**The `a = 2` U lineage's closing run**: `fRun_gen` over an empty run, then\n`closingBs` unchanged — from `TOpen₂`'s `h`-weighted U word to `WStar`, the same\nword `a ≥ 3` lands on.\n\n`closingBs` transfers because its `hj₁ : j₁ ≤ i₂` holds with equality here. Its\nsecond `bsStep` is the step the engine reports as `Y`: at `j₁ = i₂` the\nBokut–Shiao rule and Yang–Baxter share a leading word and differ by a sign, and\nthe Lean takes the monic one for the reason §4al gives.\n\nThe bystanders separate two ways, one fewer than at `a ≥ 3`: the two V words\nopen `σᵢ₋₂` against the run's `σᵢ₋₁`, and the plain U word shares that head but\nis one letter shorter than every word the run touches. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.openingPhase₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.openingPhase₂","kind":"theorem","line":12780,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12780-L12839","doc":"**The `a = 2` opening phase, whole** — `a² − 3a + 9 = 7` steps, `T0` to the\nfour-term `TOpen₂`. Four stretches rather than five: `s1`, `s2`, then `uQuad₂`\nwhere `a ≥ 3` runs a loop and a trio, then the V trio. No V loop, because at\n`jpp = i` it is the identity on `V2`.\n\nThe two lineages run U before V, as at `a ≥ 3` and for the same reason: after\n`uQuad₂` splits U in two, V is the first entry of three. Each collision\nhypothesis is one letter — U's redex opens `σᵢ₋₁` against the parked `V2`'s\n`σᵢ₋₂`, and V's `A = [σᵢ₋₂]` against both of U's outputs, which share U's\nprefix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.V2_eq_trio_source₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.V2_eq_trio_source₂","kind":"theorem","line":12766,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12766-L12778","doc":"**`V2` is the V trio's source at `a = 2`.** `descWord i j₂` opens `σᵢ`,\nwhich joins `descWord i j₁` into `bsWord₁ i j₁` and leaves `descWord i₁ j₂` —\nthe same meeting-of-two-halves as `lineage_eq_trio_source`, with the loop's\n`descWord y jpp` empty so no split is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TOpen₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TOpen₂","kind":"def","line":12747,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12747-L12764","doc":"The four words the `a = 2` opening leaves, two per lineage, `h`-weighted\nfirst in each pair — `TOpen` with `jp = i₁`, `jpp = i`, and both `trioLeft`s\ncollapsed (`U`'s to `[]`, `V`'s to `[σᵢ₋₂]`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.uQuad₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.uQuad₂","kind":"theorem","line":12696,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12696-L12720","doc":"**`a = 2`'s U-side opening**: `quadPair` applied directly to `U0`, with no\nloop and no `bsStep` before it. One term in, two out. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.U0_eq_quadPair_source₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.U0_eq_quadPair_source₂","kind":"theorem","line":12667,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12667-L12694","doc":"**At `a = 2`, `U0` IS `quadPair`'s source.** `j₁ = i₂` forces `jp = i₁` and\n`jpp = i`, and then `U0`'s three runs telescope into the braid redex with\n`L = [σ_jp, σ_jpp]` and `R = descWord jm j₂ ++ [σ_jpp]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.prefixChain₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.prefixChain₃","kind":"theorem","line":12636,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12636-L12649","doc":"**The whole `a = 3` prefix**, `a² + a + 5 = 17` steps. Same `TCancel`, same\nfive stretches; the U loop is the identity and the left split has its own\nproof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingPhase₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingPhase₃","kind":"theorem","line":12608,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12608-L12634","doc":"**`a = 3`'s closing phase.** Same `closingU_at_TOpen` and\n`closingV_at_TOpen`; only the left split is supplied differently.\n\nAt `a = 3`, `jpp = i₁` forces `jp = i₂`, and then\n`descWord i₂ jpp = descWord i₂ i₁` is **empty** while `descWord i₂ j₁` is\n`descWord jp j₁ = [σ_jp, σ_j₁]`. So `hleft` holds with both sides equal to that\ntwo-letter word — the same identity `descWord_split` gives for `a ≥ 4`, by a\ndifferent route. That is why it is a hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.prefixChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.prefixChain","kind":"theorem","line":12585,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12585-L12606","doc":"**The whole `a ≤ b` prefix** — all `a² + a + 5` steps, from the\nS-polynomial to the first cancellation.\n\n`openingPhase` is `a² − 3a + 9` of them and `closingPhase` the remaining\n`4(a − 1)`; `hecke_closing_from_topen.py` measures the two against the prefix\nlength and they close exactly, 6/6 at `a = 4, 5, 6` and `b ∈ {a, a+1}` — the\ndiagonal `b = a` included.\n\n`a = 3` is **not** covered: its loop parameter would be `m = −1`, so there is no\nloop pass at all and the opening phase's shape does not arise. It needs its own\ntreatment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TCancel_coeffEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TCancel_coeffEq","kind":"theorem","line":12562,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12562-L12583","doc":"**The cancellation.** `TCancel`'s two `WStar` entries carry `h` and `−h`, so\nthey contribute nothing; what survives is the two plain words. They are not\nadjacent — `trio` emits each lineage's `h`-weighted word immediately before its\nplain one — which is why this is `ofTerms_cancel_split` and not\n`ofTerms_cancel_pair`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingPhase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingPhase","kind":"theorem","line":12538,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12538-L12560","doc":"**The `a ≤ b` chain's closing phase** — `4(a−1)` steps, `TOpen` to `TCancel`.\n\nThe U lineage's `fRun` and two Bokut–Shiao steps, then the V lineage's `fRun`,\nwhose last step lands on the word the U side already reached. The two halves\ncompose on the nose: `closingV_at_TOpen`'s source *is* `closingU_at_TOpen`'s\ntarget, because both were stated against the same four-term list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TCancel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TCancel","kind":"def","line":12525,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12525-L12536","doc":"The chain at the prefix's first cancellation: four terms, two of them the\nsame word with opposite coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.openingPhase₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.openingPhase₃","kind":"theorem","line":12510,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12510-L12523","doc":"**`a = 3`**: the loop stretch is `openingLoops₃`. Same `TOpen`, same trios. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.openingLoops₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.openingLoops₃","kind":"theorem","line":12483,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12483-L12508","doc":"**`a = 3`'s loop stretch**: `s1`, `s2`, then the V loop alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.U0L_eq_U0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.U0L_eq_U0","kind":"theorem","line":12475,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12475-L12481","doc":"`a = 3` collapses the U loop: `jpp = i₁` empties `descWord i₂ jpp`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.openingPhase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.openingPhase","kind":"theorem","line":12447,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12447-L12458","doc":"**`a ≥ 4`**: the loop stretch is `openingLoops`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingV_at_TOpen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingV_at_TOpen","kind":"theorem","line":12259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12259-L12445","doc":"**The V lineage's closing run, in place** — `fRun` alone: the V side does not\nrun `closingBs`, because its final step *is* the cancellation. It lands on\n`WStar`, the word the U side reached two steps earlier.\n\nAll three bystanders are separated, and by three different arguments — measured\nuniform across `a = 4,5,6` and `b ∈ {a, a+1}`, for each of `fRun`'s three\nhypothesis families:\n\n* `U1` opens `σᵢ₋₁` while every word here opens `σᵢ₋₂` — **head**;\n* `V1` shares the head and is one letter short — **length**;\n* `WStar` shares head *and* length — **peel**. After cancelling the common left\n  context, every family word continues `σᵢ` (families 1 and 2) or `σ_jp, σᵢ`\n  (family 3), where `WStar` continues `σ_jp, σ_j₁`. So the discriminator is\n  `σᵢ ≠ σ_jp` or `σᵢ ≠ σ_j₁`, one letter in from the split.\n\n`WStar` is the reason the packaged `hsep` of `closingU` does not transfer: it is\nthe one bystander neither head nor length reaches. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.WStar_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.WStar_split","kind":"theorem","line":12236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12236-L12257","doc":"`WStar` split at the V run's left context. Both ends of `descWord i₂ j₁`\nare needed: `[σᵢ₋₂] ++ descWord i₁ jpp` is `σᵢ₋₂ :: σᵢ₋₁ :: descWord i₂ jpp`, and\n`descWord i₂ j₁` continues past `jpp` by exactly `[σ_jp, σ_j₁]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingU_at_TOpen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingU_at_TOpen","kind":"theorem","line":12175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12175-L12234","doc":"**`closingU` instantiated at `TOpen`** — the U lineage's run, in place, with\nthe real three bystanders.\n\nThis exists to *check that `closingU`'s hypothesis is reachable*, which the\nprevious version's was not. The discharge is the measured one: `Vh` and `V1`\nopen `σᵢ₋₂` and fail at the first letter; `U1` opens `σᵢ₋₁` and shares the whole\nleft context, so it fails on length — it is `A ++ X₀` with `|X₀|` exactly one\nshort of what `hsep` quantifies over, and taking `List.length` of both sides is\nthe whole argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingU","kind":"theorem","line":12039,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12039-L12173","doc":"**The U lineage's whole closing run**: `fRun` then `closingBs`, carrying the\nbystanders throughout, from a `TOpen` word to `WStar`.\n\n**One hypothesis covers all five obligations.** Every word this run touches has\nthe form `A ++ X` for the *same* left context `A = [σᵢ₋₁] ++ descWord i₂ jpp` and\nan `X` of the *same* length — because both rules involved are length-preserving.\nFar-commutation swaps two adjacent letters; Bokut–Shiao takes\n`descWord i j ++ [σᵢ]` to `σᵢ₋₁ :: σᵢ :: descWord (i−1) j`, and\n`|descWord i j| = |descWord (i−1) j| + 1`. So `hsep` — no bystander equals `A`\nfollowed by anything of that length — is exactly what is needed, and it is\n*discharged* differently per bystander, which is the point:\n\n* a word opening `σᵢ₋₂` fails at the first letter;\n* `U1`, which opens `σᵢ₋₁` and shares the whole context, fails on **length**: it\n  is `A ++ X₀` with `|X₀|` one short, so `List.append_cancel_left` reduces the\n  question to `|X₀| ≠ |X|`.\n\nNo length *formula* appears: the same `descWord`s occur on both sides, so `omega`\ncloses each obligation with their lengths opaque.\n\nAn earlier version of this lemma packaged the hypothesis as \"every bystander\nopens `σᵢ₋₂`\". That is **false at the call site** — the U run acts on `TOpen`'s\nthird entry, so `U1` is a bystander and opens `σᵢ₋₁` — and the lemma, though\ntrue and sorry-free, could not be applied. Sorry-freeness does not check\ninstantiability. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.WStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.WStar","kind":"def","line":12035,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12035-L12037","doc":"The word both lineages converge on: `closingBs`'s target, and the V run's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.fRun_target_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.fRun_target_eq","kind":"theorem","line":12009,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L12009-L12033","doc":"`fRun_target_eq_of_left` with the left split supplied by `descWord_split`,\nwhich is what `a ≥ 4` has: there `jpp < jppp ≤ i₁`, so `jpp ≤ y` for both\n`y = i₂` and `y = i₁`.\n\n**At `a = 3` the U lineage has `y = i₂` and `jpp = i₁ > i₂`, so this supplier\ndoes not apply** — and the identity is nonetheless true there, because\n`descWord i₂ jpp` is *empty* and `jp = i₂`. That is a different proof, not a\nweaker bound, which is why the split is a hypothesis rather than a side\ncondition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.fRun_target_eq_of_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.fRun_target_eq_of_left","kind":"theorem","line":11986,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11986-L12007","doc":"**An `fRun` target closes up into two descending runs.** Both ends rejoin:\n`descWord y jpp ++ [σ_jp, σ_j₁]` is `descWord y j₁`, and\n`descWord i jp ++ (σ_j₁ :: descWord jm j₂)` is `descWord i j₂`. Both are\n`descWord_split`; `hj₂ : j₂ ≤ j₁` is the regime, entering here as it does in\n`trio`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.trio_out_eq_fRun_source","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.trio_out_eq_fRun_source","kind":"theorem","line":11975,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11975-L11984","doc":"**A `TOpen` word is an `fRun` source.** Pure associativity once `trioLeft`\nis unfolded — `fRun`'s left context is `trioLeft` without its trailing run. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingBs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.closingBs","kind":"theorem","line":11924,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11924-L11968","doc":"**The two Bokut–Shiao steps between the closing phase's two F-runs.**\n\nAfter `fRun` the moved term reads `descWord i₁ j₁ ++ bsWord₁ i j₂`, because its\ntwo halves close up: the left context `[σᵢ₋₁] ++ descWord i₂ jpp ++ [σ_jp, σ_j₁]`\n*is* `descWord i₁ j₁`, and `descWord i j₁ ++ descWord jm j₂` is `descWord i j₂`.\nBoth are `descWord_split`, one at each end.\n\n**The two steps sit at different bottoms, and that is invisible on the\ndiagonal.** The first is at `j₂`, the second at `j₁`. When `b = a` they coincide\nand any check run only there would pass; at `b = a+1` the first redex is\n`bsWord₁ i j₂`, three letters longer. Read off the trace at `a = 6, b = 7`, not\nderived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.fRun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.fRun","kind":"theorem","line":11885,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11885-L11922","doc":"**The closing phase's F-run**, as three lemma calls rather than `2a−3`\nsteps. `S` is whatever trails the block: `σ_j₁ :: R` for the `h`-weighted term\nof a lineage and `R` for the plain one, which is the only difference between\nthem.\n\n`fRun_gen` at `D = descWord i jppp`; `htop` enters only through the run's\nclose-up, which is why the `a = 2` corner can use the general form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.fRun_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.fRun_gen","kind":"theorem","line":11808,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11808-L11883","doc":"**The F-run over an arbitrary run `D`.** `fRun` below is this at\n`D = descWord i jppp`, which is the only shape the `a ≥ 3` closing phase needs.\n\nTwo hypotheses replace `fRun`'s `jppp ≤ i`, and neither mentions `jppp`. `hD` is\nwhat the two transports actually ask of the run — every letter far enough above\n`j₁` and `jp` to commute — and `hclose` is what `descWord_split` was being used\nto produce. So the run may be **empty**, which is the `a = 2` corner: there\n`jpp = i`, `descWord i jppp` is empty, and `jppp ≤ i` is false while the run\nstill closes up (`[] ++ [σ_jpp, σ_jp]` is `descWord i jp` on the nose).\n\nSame split as `fRun_target_eq_of_left` one section down — take the list identity\nas a hypothesis, keep the `descWord_split` supplier as the named corollary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.openingPhase_of_loops","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.openingPhase_of_loops","kind":"theorem","line":11708,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11708-L11781","doc":"**The `a ≤ b` chain's opening phase, whole** — `a² − 3a + 9` steps, from the\nS-polynomial `T0` to the four-term `TOpen`.\n\nFive stretches, in the one order in which the lemmas compose: `s1`, `s2`, the U\nloop, the V loop, then `trio` twice. `hecke_opening_trio_shape.py` measures\n`2 + L + (L+1) + 6 = 2L + 9` steps and `2L + 9 = a² − 3a + 9`, so this is the\nwhole phase and nothing is left over.\n\nThe two trios run U before V, which is deg-lex's order and also the one the term\nlist forces: `openingLoops` ends at `[(V2L, 1), (U0L, −1)]`, so U is the second\nentry and V the parked one; after U's quadratic step splits it in two, V is the\nfirst entry of three. Each trio's collision hypothesis is one letter — `U`'s\nleft context opens `σᵢ₋₁` against the parked `V2L`'s `σᵢ₋₂`, and `V`'s the other\nway round against both of U's outputs, which share U's prefix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TOpen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TOpen","kind":"def","line":11691,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11691-L11706","doc":"The chain after both trios: four terms, two per lineage. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.lineage_eq_trio_source","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.lineage_eq_trio_source","kind":"theorem","line":11673,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11673-L11689","doc":"**Both lineage words open on the trio's redex.** `descWord i j₁` splits at\n`jppp`, and `descWord jpp j₂` opens with `σ_jpp`; the two halves meet as\n`bsWord₁ jpp j₁`. This is the one rewriting that turns `U0L` and `V2L` into\n`trio`'s source shape, and it is the same for both. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.trioLeft","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.trioLeft","kind":"def","line":11668,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11668-L11671","doc":"The trio's `A`, for a lineage whose leading letter is `x` and whose second\nrun starts at `y`. `U` takes `(x, y) = (i₁, i₂)`, `V` takes `(i₂, i₁)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.openingLoops","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.openingLoops","kind":"theorem","line":11620,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11620-L11666","doc":"**The `a ≤ b` chain's opening phase, loops included** — the two setup steps\nand both loops, in the one order in which they compose.\n\n`hecke_opening_coverage.py` decomposes the opening's `a² − 3a + 9` steps into\nfive stretches: the two setup steps, the U loop (`L` steps), a trio, the V loop\n(`L + 1` steps), and a second trio. This lemma is the first three of those five —\n`2 + L + (L + 1) = 2L + 3` steps — because **both loops must precede both\ntrios**, and that ordering is a constraint, not a preference.\n\n`L = (a² − 3a)/2`: measured `2, 5, 9` at `a = 4, 5, 6`, so `2L + 9` recovers the\nphase length `13, 19, 27`. It is **not** `jpp − j₁`, which this docstring said\nuntil `hecke_opening_trio_shape.py` measured it — that difference is `2` for\nevery `a`, and agrees only at `a = 4`. The loop's *level* parameter `m = a − 4`\nis the thing that is linear in `a`; its step count is not, because each level\ndescends by a pass whose own length grows.\n\nThe probe measures why. `loopTwoGenRight` (like every loop lemma here) is stated\nfor a *two-term* element, while `quadPair`, which the trios use, takes general\n`L₁`/`L₂`. Under the order the confluence engine itself produces, the U trio's\nquadratic step **splits U into two terms** before the V loop has run — at step\n6, 9 and 13 for `a = 4, 5, 6`, against V-loop completion at 9, 15 and 23 — so a\nV loop scheduled after the U trio would face three terms and no loop lemma\napplies. Running both loops first keeps the element at two terms throughout, and\nthe trios then run against the general-list `quadPair`.\n\nThat the reordering is *legal* is the same argument §4am makes for the tail: the\ntwo lineages act on different terms, so their steps commute, and\n`MultiStepReduction` fixes no order beyond each step's redex being present. Deg-lex\npicks one; the Lean is not obliged to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.TL","kind":"def","line":11615,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11615-L11618","doc":"The chain after both loops, before either trio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.trio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.trio","kind":"theorem","line":11531,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11531-L11613","doc":"**The trio**: one Bokut–Shiao step then `quadPair`, in the shape both\nlineages of the opening phase use.\n\n`hecke_opening_trio_shape.py` measures the six steps after `TL` as\n`B(jp,jpp,j₁)`, `Y(j₁,jp)`, `Q(j₁)` twice, 6/6 — and the two occurrences differ\nonly in `A` and `T`, so this is one lemma applied twice rather than a U trio and\na V trio:\n\n| | `A` | `T` |\n|---|---|---|\n| U | `[σᵢ₋₁] ++ descWord i₂ jpp ++ descWord i jppp` | `[σᵢ]` |\n| V | `[σᵢ₋₂] ++ descWord i₁ jpp ++ descWord i jppp` | `[]` |\n\nThe Bokut–Shiao redex straddles the two descending runs: `descWord i j₁` splits\nat `jppp`, leaving `descWord jpp j₁`, and `descWord jpp j₂` opens with `σ_jpp` —\nso `descWord jpp j₁ ++ [σ_jpp]` is `bsWord₁ jpp j₁`, sitting on the join. Its\nimage `bsWord₂ jp jpp j₁ = [σ_jp, σ_jpp, σ_jp, σ_j₁]` then meets `descWord jp j₂`,\nwhose first two letters are `σ_jp, σ_j₁` — and `σ_jp σ_j₁ σ_jp` followed by\n`σ_j₁` is exactly `quadPair`'s redex. Neither step creates it alone, which is\nthe same mechanism §4al describes one level down.\n\n**`hj₂ : j₂ ≤ j₁` is the regime.** It is what makes `descWord jp j₂` open with\nthose two letters, and it is `b ≥ a` — so this lemma does not instantiate in the\n`a > b` corner at all. The diagonal `b = a` is included: there `descWord j₁ j₂`\nis the single letter `σ_j₁` and `descWord jm j₂` is empty.\n\nOne collision hypothesis serves both steps: no bystander extends `A`.\n`quadPair` asks about `A ++ [σ_jp, σ_jpp]`, which is an extension of `A`, and\n`bsStep` asks about a source that begins with `A`. At both call sites it is\ndischarged by a single letter — the U trio's `A` opens `σᵢ₋₁` against the parked\n`V2L`'s `σᵢ₋₂`, and the V trio's the other way round. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.vLoop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.vLoop","kind":"theorem","line":11490,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11490-L11529","doc":"**The first term's whole loop, at general depth**, with the second parked at\nthe word its own loop left it on.\n\n`V2` is already in the loop's entry shape on the nose —\n`[σᵢ₋₂] ++ (descWord i j₁ ++ (descWord i j₂ ++ []))` — so this is\n`loopTwoGenRight` at `A = [σᵢ₋₂]`, `k = i`, `S = []`, and `m = i − jppp`. That is\none more than `uLoop`'s `m = i₁ − jppp`, which is why\n`hecke_opening_coverage.py` measures the two lineages at `L` and `L + 1` steps\nfor the same bottom `jppp`.\n\nThe two loops compose without any change of representation, and that is what\n`loopTwoGenRight` bought: `uLoop` runs `loopTwoGen`, which lists the parked term\nfirst, so it ends at `[(V2, 1), (U0L, −1)]` — V parked, U active. Here V is the\nactive one and U the parked one, so the source must list V first, which is the\nsame list. The collision hypothesis is one letter: `U0L` opens `σᵢ₋₁`, and every\nword this loop touches extends `[σᵢ₋₂]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.V2L","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.V2L","kind":"def","line":11485,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11485-L11488","doc":"The first term after its own loop, at general depth. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.uLoop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.uLoop","kind":"theorem","line":11449,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11449-L11483","doc":"**The second term's whole loop, at general depth.** `loopTwoGen` at\n`m = i₁ − jppp`, which `hecke_opening_coverage.py` measures as the U side's\nentire contribution to the opening phase — `2`, `5`, `9` steps at `a = 4, 5, 6`.\n\n`uHead` below is this at `jppp = i₁`, i.e. `m = 0`, i.e. `a = 4`. That the\ngeneral case is the same lemma at a larger `m` is why the opening phase's second\nlineage is one application rather than a chain of levels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.U0L","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.U0L","kind":"def","line":11444,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11444-L11447","doc":"The second term after its whole loop, at general depth. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.U0'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerLe.U0'","kind":"def","line":11439,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11439-L11442","doc":"The second term after its own two-step head. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.tailChainFromTwo_covers_diagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.tailChainFromTwo_covers_diagonal","kind":"theorem","line":11378,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11378-L11384","doc":"The diagonal `b = a` is inside `tailChainFromTwo`'s reach: `j₂ = j₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.tailChainFromTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.tailChainFromTwo","kind":"theorem","line":11255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11255-L11376","doc":"**The tail from the block's second level on — the diagonal included.**\n\n`tailChain` above asks `j₂ ≤ jm`, so it is off-diagonal only. This asks\n`j₂ ≤ j₁`, and at `b = a` the two coincide: the same relation `blockPass` and\n`blockPassFromTwo` stand in, one level up.\n\nNeither statement subsumes the other, because their *sources* differ. On the\ndiagonal the block is one level shorter and `blockPassFromTwo`'s source word is\nnot `blockPass`'s — the trailing `σ_jp` sits on the other side of the descending\nrun, one transport later. So this is not `tailChain` with a weakened hypothesis;\nit is the same four-step argument starting from the later word.\n\nEverything after the two blocks is *identical* to `tailChain`'s, and measurement\nsays so rather than inspection: `hecke_tail_diagonal_check.py` finds the\ndiagonal's two Bokut–Shiao steps and its endpoint word to be the same as the\noff-diagonal's, with only the block source differing — and finds the same\ncollision pattern, `hpark` failing under the engine's order at the second block\nand holding under the reordered one, 4/4 at `a = b = 3..6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.tailChain_indices_nonvacuous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.tailChain_indices_nonvacuous","kind":"theorem","line":11245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11245-L11252","doc":"The tail's index hypotheses are satisfiable, so `tailChain` is not vacuous.\nThese are `a = 4`, `b = 6` at `n = 13` — the case the probes measure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.tailChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.tailChain","kind":"theorem","line":11133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11133-L11243","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeGen_ne_of_val_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeGen_ne_of_val_ne","kind":"theorem","line":11126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11126-L11131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsStep","kind":"theorem","line":11113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11113-L11124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.resolves","kind":"theorem","line":11053,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11053-L11067","doc":"**The `a > b` corner, at every pair of depths.** The Bokut–Shiao rule at\nbottom `j₁` composed with the one at bottom `j₂`, whenever `j₁ < j₂ ≤ i − 2`,\nreduces to zero. No bound on either depth, and the chain's length — quadratic in\nthem — is carried entirely by §4af's loop. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.oc_spoly_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.oc_spoly_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":11018,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11018-L11051","doc":"**The S-polynomial** is `V0 − U0`. The two leading words cancel because the\nshort run splits as `descWord i j₂ = σᵢ :: descWord (i−1) j₂`, which is exactly\nthe overlap.\n\n**This is regime-independent, and that is worth stating.** Neither `oc` nor this\nidentity relates `j₁` to `j₂` — both ask only `j₁ ≤ i₁` and `j₂ ≤ i₁`. So the\noverlap composition and its S-polynomial are *already* established for the\n`a ≤ b` regime (`j₂ ≤ j₁`), diagonal `j₂ = j₁` included, and not only for the\n`a > b` regime this namespace's `chain` and `resolves` go on to close. What is\nregime-specific is the reduction chain from `T0` to zero, nothing before it.\n\nRecorded because the `a ≤ b` arc (bean `qou-auq3`) had been carrying\n\"`OverlapComposition` + `spoly`\" on its open list, which was wrong: both were in\nthe corpus, generic in both depths, the whole time. Verified by instantiating\nthis lemma at `j₂ ≤ j₁` and at `j₂ = j₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.oc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.oc","kind":"def","line":11002,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L11002-L11016","doc":"The composition: the Bokut–Shiao rule at the deeper bottom `j₁` against the\none at `j₂`, overlapping in the trailing `σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.chain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.chain","kind":"theorem","line":10959,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10959-L10998","doc":"**The whole chain.** Two setup steps, the second term's loop, its two closing\nsteps, then the first term's loop — and the two terms coincide. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T6_isZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T6_isZero","kind":"theorem","line":10947,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10947-L10953","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T6","kind":"def","line":10943,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10943-L10945","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T5","kind":"def","line":10940,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10940-L10941","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T4","kind":"def","line":10937,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10937-L10938","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T3","kind":"def","line":10934,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10934-L10935","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T2","kind":"def","line":10931,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10931-L10932","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T1","kind":"def","line":10928,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10928-L10929","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.T0","kind":"def","line":10925,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10925-L10926","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.s4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.s4","kind":"theorem","line":10886,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10886-L10921","doc":"**Closing step two**: the fixed-depth Bokut–Shiao rule at `(i−2, i−1, j₂−1)`,\nat the head. This lands on the word the first term's loop is heading for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.s3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.s3","kind":"theorem","line":10852,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10852-L10884","doc":"**Closing step one**: the Bokut–Shiao rule at top `i`, at the tail. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.V2_ne_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.V2_ne_cons","kind":"theorem","line":10839,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10839-L10850","doc":"The parked first term begins with `σᵢ₋₂`, the second with `σᵢ₋₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.W","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.W","kind":"def","line":10834,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10834-L10837","doc":"The word the two reductions meet at. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.U2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.U2","kind":"def","line":10829,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10829-L10832","doc":"The second term after the Bokut–Shiao step at top `i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.U1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.U1","kind":"def","line":10824,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10824-L10827","doc":"The second term after its loop. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.s2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.s2","kind":"theorem","line":10794,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10794-L10822","doc":"**Setup step two**: `σᵢσᵢ₋₂ → σᵢ₋₂σᵢ`, which puts the first term into the\nshape the loop is entered in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.s1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.s1","kind":"theorem","line":10764,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10764-L10792","doc":"**Setup step one**: the Bokut–Shiao rule at top `i−1` and the general bottom,\ninside `σᵢ · − · descWord i j₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.U0_ne_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.U0_ne_cons","kind":"theorem","line":10750,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10750-L10762","doc":"The second term begins with `σᵢ₋₁`, the first with `σᵢ`: that is all the\nsetup steps need in order to tell them apart. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.U0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.U0","kind":"def","line":10746,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10746-L10748","doc":"The S-polynomial's second term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.V2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.V2","kind":"def","line":10742,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10742-L10744","doc":"The first term parked at the loop's entry shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.V1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.V1","kind":"def","line":10737,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10737-L10740","doc":"After the Bokut–Shiao step at top `i−1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.V0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerGeneral.V0","kind":"def","line":10733,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10733-L10735","doc":"The S-polynomial's first term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopTwoGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopTwoGen","kind":"theorem","line":10676,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10676-L10701","doc":"**The loop with a parked term that is not its endpoint.**\n\n`loopTwo` carries the word the loop is heading for. The corner needs the other\narrangement too: while one term of the S-polynomial runs its loop, the other sits\nparked at a word of its own. Every word any pass rewrites has the form\n`A ++ z` — the accumulator only ever grows on the right of `A` — so a single\nhypothesis, that the parked word is not of that form, discharges every\nobligation of every pass at once. In the corner it holds for the cheapest of\nreasons: the two terms start with different letters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopTwoGenRight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopTwoGenRight","kind":"theorem","line":10656,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10656-L10674","doc":"`loopTwoGenRightSources` with the sufficient collision hypothesis, matching\n`loopTwoGen`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopTwoGenRightSources","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopTwoGenRightSources","kind":"theorem","line":10614,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10614-L10654","doc":"**The loop with the parked term listed second.** `loopListSources` at\n`L₁ = []`, `L₂ = [(P, c')]`.\n\n`AlgElement.ofTerms` is a *representation*, not a normal form: the same element\nwith its two terms in the other order is a different value, so this does not\nfollow from `loopTwoGenSources` by rearrangement — it has to be the same\ninduction against the other slot of `blockStep`'s term list, which is what\n`loopListSources` supplies.\n\nThe corner's opening phase needs exactly this. `loopTwoGen` forces the parked\nterm first, so the U-side loop ends at `[(V2, 1), (U0L, −1)]`; the V-side loop\nthat follows then has the *V* term active with the U term parked, and its source\nmust therefore list the U term first. Without this variant the two loops do not\ncompose without a change-of-representation argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopTwoGenSources","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopTwoGenSources","kind":"theorem","line":10584,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10584-L10612","doc":"**The loop with the parked term listed first**, the shape `loopTwoGen` and the\n`a > b` corner use. `loopListSources` at `L₁ = [(P, c')]`, `L₂ = []`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopListSources","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopListSources","kind":"theorem","line":10484,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10484-L10582","doc":"**The loop against an arbitrary term list, with the source-only collision\nhypothesis.**\n\nTwo generalisations of `loopTwo` at once, both forced by the corner.\n\n**Source-only collisions.** `loopTwoGen` below asks that the parked word `P` be\nno extension of `A` at all. That is sufficient — every word any pass rewrites\ndoes have the form `A ++ z` — but not necessary, and\n`hecke_prefix_head_separation.py` measures where the difference bites: at `2a`\nsteps of the corner's closing phase no choice of left context satisfies it, while\n**every source in the chain is unique**, so the precise condition holds\nthroughout.\n\nWhat the loop actually needs is that each parked word differ from the two\nfamilies `blockStep` asks about, at every level. The accumulator only ever grows\non the right of `A`, so quantifying over that growth `D` makes the hypothesis\nclosed under the recursion: descending a level replaces `D` by `σ_kd :: D`.\n\n**An arbitrary term list.** `blockStep` has taken general `L₁`/`L₂` all along;\n`loopTwo` and its descendants fixed them to `[(P, c')]` and `[]`, which puts the\nparked term *first*. `ofTerms` is a representation rather than a normal form, so\nthat choice is not free: a chain ending at `[(P, c'), (w, c)]` does not compose\nwith one starting at `[(w, c), (P, c')]`, even though the two are the same\nelement. Carrying `L₁` and `L₂` through the induction removes the choice, and\n`loopTwoGenSources` / `loopTwoGenRightSources` are the two slots. The corner's\nopening phase needs both: the U-side loop parks V and the V-side loop parks U. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopTwoFromTop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopTwoFromTop","kind":"theorem","line":10466,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10466-L10482","doc":"`loopTwo` entered at the top, where `Y` is empty. This is the shape in which\neach of the corner's two terms is actually reduced: `A` is what already sits to\nthe left of the long run, `S` what trails it (empty for the first term, `[σᵢ]` for\nthe second), and the second listed term is the word they meet at. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopTwo","kind":"theorem","line":10399,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10399-L10464","doc":"**The loop, with the S-polynomial's other term riding along.** Same walk as\n`loop`, but the element carries a second term throughout — the word the loop is\nheading for, which is what the corner's two reductions meet at. Because the\nbystander does not move (see above), it is one fixed word and the two\ndistinctness obligations of each pass are discharged uniformly by `pass_hne` and\n`pass_hcol`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.pass_hcol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.pass_hcol","kind":"theorem","line":10370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10370-L10397","doc":"The bystander is not any word the pass's transport visits. Each such word\nstarts, after `A`, with a letter of the run above `k`, and every one of those is\nmore than one above `σ_kd`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.pass_hne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.pass_hne","kind":"theorem","line":10347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10347-L10368","doc":"The bystander is not the word the pass rewrites. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.append_cons_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.append_cons_ne","kind":"theorem","line":10339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10339-L10345","doc":"Two words with a common prefix differ as soon as the next letter does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopFromTop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loopFromTop","kind":"theorem","line":10307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10307-L10320","doc":"**The loop, entered at the top.** The first pass has `k = i`, so nothing of\nthe long run lies above it and `Y` is empty; `m` is the number of passes less one.\nThis is the form the corner's two terms are actually reduced by, and it witnesses\nthat `loop`'s hypotheses are satisfiable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.loop","kind":"theorem","line":10242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10242-L10305","doc":"**The loop.** `blockStep` iterated: `k` walks down from its starting value to\n`e`, one pass per index, and what those passes leave behind is the descending run\n`descWord kd ed` accumulated in front.\n\nThe induction is on the number of passes still to come. It carries `Y` — the part\nof the long run lying above `k` — as a parameter rather than as `descWord i (k+1)`,\nso each pass hands the next one `Y ++ [σ_k]` and no index above `k` is ever named.\n\nStated for a single term, where the collision hypotheses of `blockStep` are\nvacuous. That is the whole combinatorial content of the `a > b` corner: what\nremains for the two-term S-polynomial is bookkeeping about which words the\nbystanding term must avoid, not further rewriting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.blockStep_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.blockStep_top","kind":"theorem","line":10220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10220-L10240","doc":"**The loop's first pass**, where `k = i` and nothing lies above it: `Y` is\nempty and the transport is the identity, so the pass is the Bokut–Shiao step\nalone. Only two non-collision facts are needed, one per endpoint — with `Y` empty\nthe transport passes through no intermediate word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.blockStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CornerBlock.blockStep","kind":"theorem","line":10166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10166-L10218","doc":"**One pass of the corner loop**: a Bokut–Shiao step at top `k`, then the\nnewly exposed `σ_{k−1}` carried left across `Y`.\n\n`Y` is the part of the long run `descWord i j₁` lying above `k`; `R` is whatever\nhas already accumulated to the left, `S` whatever trails on the right (empty on\nthe `V` side, `[σᵢ]` on the `U` side). The two collision hypotheses are the ones\n`monicStep` and `farComm_transport_left` ask for: the other terms of the element\nmust miss the word being rewritten, and must miss every word the transport passes\nthrough. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_cons_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_cons_le","kind":"theorem","line":10149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10149-L10160","doc":"`descWord_cons` at the boundary. The original needs the floor to lie at or\nbelow `i − 1`; this needs it only at or below `i`, the extra case being `j = i`,\nwhere the tail is empty rather than a shorter run. The corner loop's last pass\nis exactly that case, so it cannot use the original. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":10141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10141-L10147","doc":"A descending run from below its own floor is empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoCornerDepth3.resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoCornerDepth3.resolves","kind":"theorem","line":10060,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10060-L10092","doc":"**23 steps, to zero, at every depth `j ≤ i − 4`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoCornerDepth3.oc_spoly_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoCornerDepth3.oc_spoly_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":10035,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10035-L10058","doc":"**The S-polynomial.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoCornerDepth3.oc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoCornerDepth3.oc","kind":"def","line":10022,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10022-L10033","doc":"The composition of the rule at the general depth `j` with the rule at\ndepth `3`, overlapping in the trailing `σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoCornerDepth3.T23_isZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoCornerDepth3.T23_isZero","kind":"theorem","line":10013,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L10013-L10020","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoCornerDepth3.s23","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoCornerDepth3.s23","kind":"theorem","line":9989,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L9989-L10009","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoCornerDepth3.s22","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoCornerDepth3.s22","kind":"theorem","line":9967,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L9967-L9987","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoCornerDepth3.s21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoCornerDepth3.s21","kind":"theorem","line":9945,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/u