n","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S9","kind":"def","line":5536,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5536-L5539","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S8","kind":"def","line":5531,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5531-L5534","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S7","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S7","kind":"def","line":5526,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5526-L5529","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S6","kind":"def","line":5520,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5520-L5524","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S5","kind":"def","line":5514,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5514-L5518","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S4","kind":"def","line":5508,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5508-L5512","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S3","kind":"def","line":5502,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5502-L5506","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S2","kind":"def","line":5496,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5496-L5500","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S1","kind":"def","line":5491,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5491-L5494","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.S0","kind":"def","line":5487,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5487-L5489","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v12","kind":"def","line":5482,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5482-L5483","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v11","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v11","kind":"def","line":5479,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5479-L5480","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v10","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v10","kind":"def","line":5476,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5476-L5477","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v9","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v9","kind":"def","line":5473,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5473-L5474","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v8","kind":"def","line":5470,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5470-L5471","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v7","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v7","kind":"def","line":5467,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5467-L5468","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v6","kind":"def","line":5464,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5464-L5465","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v5","kind":"def","line":5461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5461-L5462","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v4","kind":"def","line":5458,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5458-L5459","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v3","kind":"def","line":5454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5454-L5456","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v2","kind":"def","line":5451,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5451-L5452","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.v1","kind":"def","line":5448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5448-L5449","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.w2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.w2","kind":"def","line":5443,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5443-L5446","doc":"`σᵢ₋₁ σᵢ σᵢ₋₁ σᵢ₋₁ T σᵢ` — the second. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.w1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidBokutShiao.w1","kind":"def","line":5438,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5438-L5441","doc":"`σᵢ σᵢ₋₁ σᵢ₋₁ σᵢ σᵢ₋₁ T` — the first term of the S-polynomial. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_head","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_head","kind":"theorem","line":5415,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5415-L5426","doc":"**The descending run begins with its top index**, whenever it is non-empty.\nSplits on `j = i` (`descWord_self`) and `j < i` (`descWord_cons` at `i − 1`). ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quadPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quadPair","kind":"theorem","line":5378,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5378-L5413","doc":"**The Yang–Baxter step and the quadratic step it sets up.** One term in, two\nout, with the `h`-weighted one first. `L` and `R` are arbitrary: the pair occurs\ntwice in the prefix and the two occurrences differ only in them. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.blockPass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.blockPass","kind":"theorem","line":5330,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5330-L5353","doc":"**The block, at general depth, off the diagonal.** One pass of the `a ≤ b`\nregime's far-commutation block when `j₂ < j₁`: the first level below the cap,\nthen `blockPassFromTwo` for the rest.\n\nThe left context `A` and the trailing word `T` are both arbitrary — the block\nnever has to know what the prefix left on either side of it. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.blockPassSources","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.blockPassSources","kind":"theorem","line":5285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5285-L5328","doc":"**The block off the diagonal, with the source-only collision hypothesis.**\nThree families: the leading `σ_jp` transport across `descWord jm j₂`, plus the\ntwo `blockPassFromTwoSources` asks. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.blockPassFromTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.blockPassFromTwo","kind":"theorem","line":5258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5258-L5283","doc":"**The block from its second level on.** The two levels below the cap are\n`h = j₁+1` and `h = j₁+2`; this covers the second and everything above it, which\nis all of the block when the first level is absent.\n\nIt asks only `j₂ ≤ j₁`, **not** `j₂ < j₁`, and that is the point: at `b = a` the\ntwo coincide, so a lemma demanding the strict inequality cannot be instantiated\non the diagonal at all. The trailing word `T` is a parameter for the same\nreason — see §4aj. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.blockPassFromTwoSources","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.blockPassFromTwoSources","kind":"theorem","line":5209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5209-L5256","doc":"**The block from its second level on, with the source-only collision\nhypothesis.** Two families, one per underlying transport: the `σ_jpp` step\nacross `descWord j₁ j₂`, and the block carried across `descWord jp j₂`. See\n`blockTransportRightSources` (§4ai) for why `hpark` is stronger than needed. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.blockTransportRight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.blockTransportRight","kind":"theorem","line":5137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5137-L5152","doc":"The block transport with the unrestricted hypothesis — `hpark` supplies\nevery case of the source family at once. Kept because §4aj's callers already\nsupply it, exactly as `farComm_transport_right` is kept for §4y's. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.blockTransportRightSources","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.blockTransportRightSources","kind":"theorem","line":5075,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5075-L5135","doc":"**A whole block carried rightwards past a run, with the source-only\ncollision hypothesis.** `X` and `W` swap, provided every letter of `X` is at\nleast two above every letter of `W`, inside any context and at any position of\nthe term list.\n\nThe induction peels `X` from the **right**: its last letter transports across\n`W` first and then joins `B`, so the recursion re-enters with `X` one shorter\nand `B` one longer. Peeling from the left would not compose — the head of `X`\nis separated from `W` by the rest of `X`, so no single transport applies.\n\n`hpark` below — no other term extends `A` — is *sufficient* but not necessary,\nand `hecke_prefix_head_separation.py` measures where the difference bites: at\n`2a` steps of the corner's closing phase no choice of left context satisfies\n`hpark`, while **every source in the chain is unique**, so the precise condition\nholds throughout.\n\nWhat the transport actually needs is that no other term equal a word it\n*rewrites*. Peeling `X` from the right, those are exactly\n\n    A ++ P ++ u ++ (x :: (v ++ (S ++ B)))    for  P ++ (x :: S) = X,\n                                                   u ++ v = W,  v ≠ []\n\n— one per letter of `X` and per interior split of `W`. The `v ≠ []` exclusion is\n`farComm_transport_right_sources`'s own (§4ah): it drops the split naming each\ntransport's final word, which is produced and never rewritten. This lemma\nthreads that family through the recursion instead of over-approximating it. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_transport_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_transport_right","kind":"theorem","line":5031,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L5031-L5048","doc":"The rightward transport with the unrestricted collision hypothesis — every\nsplit of `w`, including the one naming the final word. Weaker than\n`farComm_transport_right_sources` and kept for §4y's callers, exactly as\n`farComm_transport_left` is kept for §4v's. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_transport_right_sources","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_transport_right_sources","kind":"theorem","line":4958,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4958-L5029","doc":"**Far-commutation transport, rightwards, at any list position.** The mirror\nof `farComm_transport_left_sources`: there a generator below the block moves\nleft, here a generator above it moves right. The induction recurses on the head\nof `w` and prepends its step, the opposite end from the leftward version.\n\nAs on the left, the collision hypothesis enumerates the intermediate words by\nsplitting `w`, and one of those splits names the transport's own *final* word,\nwhich the proof never needs. **On this side that split is `v = []`, not\n`u = []`** — the two ends swap with the direction of travel, since here the\nmoving letter starts at the left of `w` and finishes at its right. Concretely\n`hcol` is used at `u = []` with `v = y :: w` for the single step, which is\nnon-empty, and the recursion passes `v` through untouched.\n\nThe distinction matters because the bystanding term of the corner chain *is*\nthe transport's final word, so the unrestricted hypothesis is false exactly\nwhere the transport is needed — the same trap §4v hit on the left, and it would\nbe hit again here by mirroring the wrong end. `farComm_transport_right` below is\nthis with the stronger hypothesis, kept because §4y's callers already supply\nit. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.bokutShiao_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.bokutShiao_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":4931,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4931-L4939","doc":"**Against Bokut–Shiao at `j = i − 1`.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.yangBaxter_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.yangBaxter_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":4921,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4921-L4929","doc":"**Against Yang–Baxter.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.oc_reduces_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.oc_reduces_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":4880,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4880-L4912","doc":"**Nine steps, to zero.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.oc_spoly_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.oc_spoly_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":4851,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4851-L4878","doc":"**The S-polynomial**, in the two-term shape the chain starts from. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.stage_self_isZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.stage_self_isZero","kind":"theorem","line":4840,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4840-L4849","doc":"The chain's endpoint is coefficientwise zero: the same word with opposite\ncoefficients. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain9","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain9","kind":"theorem","line":4819,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4819-L4836","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain8","kind":"theorem","line":4798,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4798-L4817","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain7","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain7","kind":"theorem","line":4778,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4778-L4796","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain6","kind":"theorem","line":4757,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4757-L4776","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain5","kind":"theorem","line":4738,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4738-L4755","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain4","kind":"theorem","line":4717,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4717-L4736","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain3","kind":"theorem","line":4697,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4697-L4715","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain2","kind":"theorem","line":4678,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4678-L4695","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.chain1","kind":"theorem","line":4656,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4656-L4676","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.gen_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.gen_ne","kind":"theorem","line":4645,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4645-L4654","doc":"The three generators in play are pairwise distinct, which is the only\nword-distinctness the whole section needs. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.braid_hlm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.braid_hlm","kind":"theorem","line":4628,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4628-L4631","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.braid_hrel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.braid_hrel","kind":"theorem","line":4618,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4618-L4626","doc":"The braid rule at the lower level, which is the Bokut–Shiao rule at\n`j = i − 2`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.far_hrel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.far_hrel","kind":"theorem","line":4611,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4611-L4616","doc":"Far-commutation between the top generator and the one two below it. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.outer_hlm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.outer_hlm","kind":"theorem","line":4604,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4604-L4609","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.outer_hrel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.outer_hrel","kind":"theorem","line":4593,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4593-L4602","doc":"The outer Bokut–Shiao rule, in the same form. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.lower_hlm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.lower_hlm","kind":"theorem","line":4588,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4588-L4591","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.lower_hrel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.lower_hrel","kind":"theorem","line":4579,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4579-L4586","doc":"The lower Bokut–Shiao rule, in the two-word form `monicStep` wants. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.stage","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.stage","kind":"def","line":4570,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4570-L4573","doc":"Stage `k` of the chain: the live term, the passenger, and the coefficient. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.B3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.B3","kind":"def","line":4565,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4565-L4568","doc":"After the outer rule; one braid straightening from `A₅`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.B2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.B2","kind":"def","line":4560,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4560-L4563","doc":"After commuting `σᵢ` past `σᵢ₋₂`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.B1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.B1","kind":"def","line":4555,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4555-L4558","doc":"After the first Bokut–Shiao application. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.B0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.B0","kind":"def","line":4550,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4550-L4553","doc":"Stage words of the second term. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.A5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.A5","kind":"def","line":4545,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4545-L4548","doc":"**The common endpoint of both branches.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.A4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.A4","kind":"def","line":4540,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4540-L4543","doc":"After the second Bokut–Shiao application. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.A3","kind":"def","line":4535,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4535-L4538","doc":"After the outer rule. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.A2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.A2","kind":"def","line":4530,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4530-L4533","doc":"After commuting `σᵢ` past `σᵢ₋₂`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.A1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.A1","kind":"def","line":4525,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4525-L4528","doc":"After the first Bokut–Shiao application. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.A0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.A0","kind":"def","line":4521,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4521-L4523","doc":"Stage words of the first term. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.oc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoBraid.oc","kind":"def","line":4500,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4500-L4513","doc":"The composition of `bokutShiaoRelation i' i j₁` with a rule leading on the\nbraid word `σᵢσᵢ₋₁σᵢ`, overlapping in the trailing `σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quadStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quadStep","kind":"theorem","line":4461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4461-L4494","doc":"**One step of a chain, by the quadratic rule.** Unlike `monicStep` the\noutput has one more term than the input: the quadratic rule has three words, so\nthe targeted term is replaced by two, with coefficients `c·(q − q⁻¹)` and `c`.\n\nThe contexts `a`, `b` and the surrounding terms `L₁`, `L₂` are arbitrary, and\n`W` is tied to the rule's leading word by an equation rather than being it on\nthe nose, so consecutive steps compose without their decompositions having to\nagree syntactically — the same reason `monicStep` is stated that way. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.monicStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.monicStep","kind":"theorem","line":4400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4400-L4438","doc":"**One step of a two-term chain, by a monic two-word rule.** The stage words\nare arbitrary and tied to the rule's by equations, so consecutive steps compose\nwithout the decompositions having to agree syntactically. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.resolves","kind":"theorem","line":4325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4325-L4344","doc":"**The family, at the indices the enumeration presents it with.** `jup` names\n`j₀ + 1`; the two splits of the descending run come from `descWord_split`, and\n`A'` is the piece above `j₀`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.oc_reduces_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.oc_reduces_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":4211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4211-L4323","doc":"**Five stages, to zero.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.chainStep5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.chainStep5","kind":"theorem","line":4157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4157-L4207","doc":"Step 5 — the outer rule, in the context `(σ_{j₀'} ∣ ε)`, landing on zero. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.chainStep3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.chainStep3","kind":"theorem","line":4109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4109-L4155","doc":"Step 3 — the inner rule again, now in the second term. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.chainStep1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.chainStep1","kind":"theorem","line":4057,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4057-L4107","doc":"Step 1 — the inner Bokut–Shiao rule, in the context `(σᵢ A' ∣ σᵢ)`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.T4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.T4","kind":"def","line":4043,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4043-L4051","doc":"Stage `4` — both terms now begin with `σ_{j₀'}`, and what follows is the\nouter rule's two words. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.T3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.T3","kind":"def","line":4034,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4034-L4041","doc":"Stage `3` — the inner rule has fired in the second term too. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.T2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.T2","kind":"def","line":4024,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4024-L4032","doc":"Stage `2` — `σ_{j₀'}` has crossed the upper run, so the first term is\n`σ_{j₀'} :: bsWord₁ i j`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.T1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommInner.T1","kind":"def","line":4015,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4015-L4022","doc":"Stage `1` — the inner Bokut–Shiao rule has fired in the first term. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_split","kind":"theorem","line":4004,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L4004-L4009","doc":"`descWord i j = descWord i k ++ descWord k' j` whenever `k' + 1 = k` and the\nsplit point lies inside the run. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_split_aux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_split_aux","kind":"theorem","line":3977,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3977-L4002","doc":"**The descending run splits at any interior index.** Proved by walking the\nbottom index down with `descWord_snoc`, so the induction is on the gap\n`k' − j` rather than on `List.finRange`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.yangBaxter_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.yangBaxter_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":3886,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3886-L3930","doc":"**Yang–Baxter**, which exists only at `j = i − 1`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.bokutShiao_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.bokutShiao_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":3853,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3853-L3884","doc":"**Bokut–Shiao**, at any `j` with `j₀ + 1 < j`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.bsWord₂_index_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.bsWord₂_index_ge","kind":"theorem","line":3841,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3841-L3851","doc":"Every letter of `bsWord₂ i' i j` has index at least `j`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.oc_reduces_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.oc_reduces_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":3758,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3758-L3833","doc":"**Two leftward transports and one rule application, to zero.**\n\nEvery side condition reduces to the two letter inequalities `q ≠ σᵢ` and\n`q ≠ σ_{j₀}`: the rule's other word begins with a letter that is neither the top\nof the run nor the travelling generator, which is what keeps it distinguishable\nfrom every intermediate word of both transports. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.chainStep3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.chainStep3","kind":"theorem","line":3719,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3719-L3756","doc":"Phase 3 — the rule itself, in the context `(σ_{j₀} ∣ ε)`, landing on zero.\nThe one distinctness needed is the first letter: the rule's other word begins\nwith `q`, its leading monomial with `σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.oc_spoly_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.oc_spoly_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":3695,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3695-L3717","doc":"**The S-polynomial.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.E2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.E2","kind":"def","line":3687,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3687-L3693","doc":"Stage `2` — and the rule's other word too, so the first term is now the\nleading monomial in the context `(σ_{j₀} ∣ ε)`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.E1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.E1","kind":"def","line":3680,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3680-L3685","doc":"Stage `1` — `σ_{j₀}` has crossed the descending run. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.E0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.E0","kind":"def","line":3672,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3672-L3678","doc":"Stage `0` — the S-polynomial. The ambient word cancels; each surviving term\ncarries a stray `σ_{j₀}`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.oc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicFarCommLow.oc","kind":"def","line":3656,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3656-L3670","doc":"The composition of a rule leading on `σᵢ D' σᵢ` with the far-commutation rule\n`σᵢ σ_{j₀}`, overlapping in the trailing `σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_transport_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_transport_left","kind":"theorem","line":3634,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3634-L3650","doc":"The transport with the unrestricted collision hypothesis — every split of `w`,\nincluding the one naming the final word. Weaker than\n`farComm_transport_left_sources` and kept for §4v's callers. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_transport_left_sources","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_transport_left_sources","kind":"theorem","line":3562,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3562-L3632","doc":"**Far-commutation transport, leftwards.** If every letter of `w` is strictly\nmore than one above `σ_z`, then `σ_z` may be walked from the right end of `w` to\nits left end, one far-commutation application per letter, inside any contexts\n`a`, `b` and at any position of the term list.\n\nThe induction recurses on the *head* of `w` and appends its step at the end,\nwhich is the opposite end from `farComm_transport`: there the moving letter\nleads, here it trails. The collision hypothesis enumerates the intermediate words\nby splitting `w`, exactly as in §4u.\n\nThat enumeration includes the split `u = []`, which names the transport's *final*\nword — and the proof never uses it: `hcol` is applied only with a cons-headed\nfirst argument, and the `nil` case discards it outright. So `u ≠ []` suffices,\nand it matters. In the corner chain of §4af the bystanding term *is* the final\nword, so the unrestricted hypothesis is false exactly where the transport is\nneeded. `farComm_transport_left` below is this with the stronger hypothesis,\nkept because §4v's callers already supply it. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ofTerms_cancel_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ofTerms_cancel_pair","kind":"theorem","line":3546,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3546-L3560","doc":"**Two terms on one word with opposite coefficients contribute nothing.**\nThe bridge between the chain's term list before and after a cancellation. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ofTerms_cancel_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ofTerms_cancel_split","kind":"theorem","line":3515,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3515-L3543","doc":"**Two terms on one word with opposite coefficients contribute nothing, even\nwith other terms between them.**\n\nThe adjacent case is what §4ak's cancellations need at the top level; the\n`a ≤ b` closing phase needs the split one. There the four-term element is\n`[(Vh, h), (V1, 1), (Uh, −h), (U1, −1)]`, and the two terms that reconverge are\nthe two `h`-weighted ones — with `(V1, 1)` sitting between them. That ordering\nis not a choice: `trio` emits its `h`-weighted word immediately before its plain\none, in place, so the two lineages interleave as `V, V, U, U`.\n\n`ofTerms_cancel_pair` is this at `M = []`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ofTerms_coeff_mid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.ofTerms_coeff_mid","kind":"theorem","line":3476,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3476-L3492","doc":"The coefficient of one singled-out term of an `ofTerms` list, when no other\nterm carries the same word. Stating the transport for a term at an arbitrary\nposition needs exactly this. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_index_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_index_ge","kind":"theorem","line":3465,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3465-L3474","doc":"Every letter of `descWord i j` has index at least `j` — the lower bound to\n`descWord_index_le`, and what makes each letter a far-commutation partner of a\ngenerator strictly below `j`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.yangBaxter_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.yangBaxter_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":3379,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3379-L3420","doc":"**Yang–Baxter**: `u'' = [σ_{m−1}, σ_m]`, `w₂ = σ_{m−1}σ_mσ_{m−1}`, `c = −1`.\nIts two terms are listed in the opposite order, hence the coefficientwise\n`hrel`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.bokutShiao_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.bokutShiao_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":3347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3347-L3377","doc":"**Bokut–Shiao**: `u'' = descWord m−1 j ++ [σ_m]`, `w₂ = bsWord₂`, `c = 1`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.bsWord₂_index_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.bsWord₂_index_le","kind":"theorem","line":3335,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3335-L3345","doc":"Every letter of `bsWord₂ m' m j` has index at most `m`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.oc_reduces_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.oc_reduces_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":3268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3268-L3327","doc":"**Two transports and one rule application, to zero.**\n\n`hfar₂` and `hfaru` are the two far-commutation blanket conditions: every letter\nof the rule's other word, and of the tail of its leading monomial, is far below\n`σₓ`. For both instances they follow from `m + 1 < x` and the fact that no letter\nof either word has index above `m`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.chainStep3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.chainStep3","kind":"theorem","line":3233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3233-L3266","doc":"Phase 3 — the rule itself, in the context `(ε ∣ σₓ)`, landing on zero. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.oc_spoly_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.oc_spoly_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":3211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3211-L3231","doc":"**The S-polynomial.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.E2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.E2","kind":"def","line":3203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3203-L3209","doc":"Stage `2` — `σₓ` has crossed `u''` too, so the second term is the rule's\nleading monomial with `σₓ` appended. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.E1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.E1","kind":"def","line":3196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3196-L3201","doc":"Stage `1` — `σₓ` has crossed `w₂`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.E0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.E0","kind":"def","line":3188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3188-L3194","doc":"Stage `0` — the S-polynomial, two terms; the ambient word `σₓ σ_m u''` is\nreached from both sides and cancels. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.oc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.FarCommCyclic.oc","kind":"def","line":3173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3173-L3186","doc":"The composition of `farCommRelation x m` with a rule whose leading monomial\nbegins with `σ_m`, overlapping in that letter. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_transport_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_transport_fst","kind":"theorem","line":3119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3119-L3167","doc":"**Transport with a bystander, moving term second.** The mirror of\n`farComm_transport_snd` in the list slot, not in the direction of travel. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_transport_snd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_transport_snd","kind":"theorem","line":3068,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3068-L3117","doc":"**Transport with a bystander, moving term first.** The collision hypothesis\nis stated over every splitting `u ++ v = w`, because that enumerates exactly the\nintermediate words the run passes through: `σₓ` sits after `u` and before `v`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.resolves","kind":"theorem","line":3012,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L3012-L3022","doc":"**The family, in the form the enumeration meets it.** `v` is `descWord i−2 j`,\nwhich exists exactly when `j < i − 1` — the condition §4q's cyclic hypothesis\nfails under, so this covers precisely what §4q leaves open. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.oc_reduces_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.oc_reduces_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":2993,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2993-L3010","doc":"**Three fixed steps, then `|v|` far-commutation steps, to zero.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.chainStep3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.chainStep3","kind":"theorem","line":2933,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2933-L2991","doc":"Step 3 — the rule's own relation in empty context, spending the `h` term.\nThe only distinctness here that is not a length count: `bsWord₁` and `bsWord₂`\nhave the same length and are separated by their first letter. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.chainStep2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.chainStep2","kind":"theorem","line":2891,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2891-L2931","doc":"Step 2 — the quadratic rule at `i − 1`, on the `σᵢ₋₁σᵢ₋₁` the braid step\nleft, in the context `(σᵢ₋₁σᵢ ∣ v)`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.chainStep1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.chainStep1","kind":"theorem","line":2849,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2849-L2889","doc":"Step 1 — Yang–Baxter, in the context `(ε ∣ σᵢ₋₁ v)`. Its leading coefficient\nis `−1`, so the step coefficient is `−1` too. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.oc_spoly_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.oc_spoly_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":2818,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2818-L2847","doc":"**The S-polynomial.** `Q_i`'s leading term and the rule's leading term are\nboth the ambient word `σᵢσᵢσᵢ₋₁vσᵢ`, so they cancel without any word-distinctness\nargument; three terms survive. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.G4_isZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.G4_isZero","kind":"theorem","line":2809,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2809-L2816","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.G4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.G4","kind":"def","line":2801,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2801-L2807","doc":"Stage `4` — what the transport lands on: two equal words with opposite\ncoefficients, coefficientwise zero. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.G3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.G3","kind":"def","line":2793,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2793-L2799","doc":"Stage `3` — one generator on the wrong side of `v`, and nothing else. This is\nexactly `farComm_transport`'s starting shape with `a = [σᵢ₋₁]`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.G2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.G2","kind":"def","line":2782,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2782-L2791","doc":"Stage `2` — the square is out; the `h` term it leaves is `bsWord₂`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.G1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.G1","kind":"def","line":2772,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2772-L2780","doc":"Stage `1` — the braid is straightened. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.G0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.G0","kind":"def","line":2762,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2762-L2770","doc":"Stage `0` — the S-polynomial. The ambient word `σᵢσᵢσᵢ₋₁vσᵢ` cancels. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.bs_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.QuadBokutShiao.bs_lm","kind":"theorem","line":2753,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2753-L2760","doc":"The rule's leading monomial, in the form §4q's `oc` wants: it begins with\n`σᵢ`, and the tail is `σᵢ₋₁ v σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farComm_transport","kind":"theorem","line":2687,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2687-L2747","doc":"**Far-commutation transport.** If every letter of `w` commutes far with `σₓ`,\nthen `c · (a σₓ w) − c · (a w σₓ)` reduces, in `|w|` steps, to an element that is\ncoefficientwise zero — one far-commutation application per letter, each in the\ncontext accumulated so far.\n\nStated for an arbitrary `w` and an arbitrary left context `a`, because the\ninduction has to move `a` anyway: the letter just passed becomes part of the\ncontext for the next step. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_index_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_index_le","kind":"theorem","line":2677,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2677-L2685","doc":"Every letter of `descWord i j` has index at most `i`. The bound the transport\nneeds: it is what makes each letter of `v` a far-commutation partner of `σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.resolves","kind":"theorem","line":2618,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2618-L2628","doc":"**The family, in the form the enumeration meets it.** The hypothesis is the\nfar-commutation side condition `j + 1 < i` and nothing else: it is what makes\n`σᵢσⱼ` a rule of the system, and simultaneously what makes `jp = j + 1` a legal\nBokut–Shiao depth for step 4. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.oc_reduces_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.oc_reduces_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":2600,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2600-L2616","doc":"**Four steps, to zero.** `reducesToZero_congr` (§6) joins the chain, which\nruns on `F₀`, to the S-polynomial, which `oc_spoly_coeff` says is `F₀`\ncoefficientwise. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.chainStep4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.chainStep4","kind":"theorem","line":2566,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2566-L2598","doc":"Step 4 — the family's own rule at depth `jp`, in empty context. `F₃` *is*\nthat relation, so the step lands on zero. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.chainStep3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.chainStep3","kind":"theorem","line":2522,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2522-L2564","doc":"Step 3 — the family's own rule at depth `j`, in empty context, clearing the\n`h` term the two squares left. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.chainStep2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.chainStep2","kind":"theorem","line":2494,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2494-L2520","doc":"Step 2 — the quadratic rule at `j` again, now in the context\n`(σᵢ₋₁ descWord i jp ∣ ε)`; that prefix *is* `bsWord₂ i' i jp`, by\n`descWord_cons`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.chainStep1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.chainStep1","kind":"theorem","line":2468,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2468-L2492","doc":"Step 1 — the quadratic rule at `j`, in the context `(descWord i jp ∣ σᵢ)`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.oc_spoly_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.oc_spoly_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":2444,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2444-L2466","doc":"**The S-polynomial.** The ambient word `descWord i j ++ [σᵢ, σⱼ]` is reached\nfrom both sides and cancels identically; `descWord_snoc` then exhibits what\nsurvives as `F₀`, with the square visible in both terms. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.F3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.F3","kind":"def","line":2437,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2437-L2442","doc":"Stage `3` — exactly the Bokut–Shiao relation at `jp`, which annihilates it. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.F2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.F2","kind":"def","line":2427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2427-L2435","doc":"Stage `2` — both squares out. What is left is `h ·` the Bokut–Shiao relation\nat `j`, plus the Bokut–Shiao relation at `jp`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.F1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.F1","kind":"def","line":2419,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2419-L2425","doc":"Stage `1` — the square in the first term is out. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.F0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.F0","kind":"def","line":2412,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2412-L2417","doc":"Stage `0` — the S-polynomial. Both terms end in `σⱼσⱼ`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.head_ne'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.head_ne'","kind":"theorem","line":2400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2400-L2405","doc":"`head_ne` the other way round; both directions occur, because the targeted\nword is sometimes on the left of the comparison and sometimes on the right. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.head_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.head_ne","kind":"theorem","line":2387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2387-L2398","doc":"**The one word-distinctness fact the chain needs.** `descWord i jp` begins\nwith `σᵢ` (`descWord_cons`), and every `bsWord₂`-side word of the chain begins\nwith `σᵢ₋₁`; no length arithmetic and no knowledge of the tail is involved. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.oc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarCommSame.oc","kind":"def","line":2373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2373-L2385","doc":"The composition of `bokutShiaoRelation i' i j` with `farCommRelation i j`,\noverlapping in the single letter `σᵢ` — the same shape as §4o, with the\nfar-commutation rule's bottom index moved up to `j`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.bs_bs_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.bs_bs_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":2315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2315-L2324","doc":"**Bokut–Shiao against Bokut–Shiao.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.bs_yb_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.bs_yb_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":2304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2304-L2313","doc":"**Bokut–Shiao against Yang–Baxter.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.yb_bs_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.yb_bs_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":2294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2294-L2302","doc":"**Yang–Baxter against Bokut–Shiao.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.yb_yb_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.yb_yb_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":2284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2284-L2292","doc":"**Yang–Baxter against Yang–Baxter.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.bs_hlm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.bs_hlm","kind":"theorem","line":2280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2280-L2282","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.yb_hlm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.yb_hlm","kind":"theorem","line":2276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2276-L2278","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.bs_hrel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.bs_hrel","kind":"theorem","line":2270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2270-L2274","doc":"The Bokut–Shiao rule at `j = i − 1`, at `c = 1`. Same terms, same order. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.yb_hrel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.yb_hrel","kind":"theorem","line":2258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2258-L2268","doc":"The Yang–Baxter rule in the shape §4r wants, at `c = −1`. Its two terms are\nlisted in the opposite order, hence the coefficientwise statement. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.oc_reduces_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.oc_reduces_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":2211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2211-L2246","doc":"**Eight steps, to zero.**\n\n`reducesToZero_congr` (§6) makes the last join: the chain runs on `F₀`, and\n`oc_spoly_coeff` says the S-polynomial is coefficientwise `F₀`. That congruence\nwas built for the negation transfer; this is where it first pays. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep8","kind":"theorem","line":2192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2192-L2209","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep7","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep7","kind":"theorem","line":2173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2173-L2190","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep6","kind":"theorem","line":2154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2154-L2171","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep5","kind":"theorem","line":2135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2135-L2152","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep4","kind":"theorem","line":2105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2105-L2133","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep3","kind":"theorem","line":2075,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2075-L2103","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep2","kind":"theorem","line":2056,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2056-L2073","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.chainStep1","kind":"theorem","line":2037,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2037-L2054","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F7","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F7","kind":"def","line":2029,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2029-L2035","doc":"Stage `7` of the chain. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F6","kind":"def","line":2020,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2020-L2027","doc":"Stage `6` of the chain. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F5","kind":"def","line":2010,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2010-L2018","doc":"Stage `5` of the chain. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F4","kind":"def","line":2001,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L2001-L2008","doc":"Stage `4` of the chain. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F3","kind":"def","line":1992,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1992-L1999","doc":"Stage `3` of the chain. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F2","kind":"def","line":1983,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1983-L1990","doc":"Stage `2` of the chain. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F1","kind":"def","line":1975,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1975-L1981","doc":"Stage `1` of the chain. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.F0","kind":"def","line":1968,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1968-L1973","doc":"Stage `0` of the chain — the S-polynomial. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.oc_spoly_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.oc_spoly_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":1928,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1928-L1956","doc":"**The S-polynomial: two terms, and the leading coefficients enter only as\ntheir product.** The ambient word `σᵢσᵢ₋₁σᵢσᵢ₋₁σᵢ` is reached from both sides and\ncancels. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.oc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.oc","kind":"def","line":1913,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1913-L1926","doc":"The composition of two rules that both lead on `σᵢσᵢ₋₁σᵢ`, overlapping in the\nmiddle letter — the braid relation against itself. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.wLo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.wLo","kind":"def","line":1910,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1910-L1911","doc":"`σᵢ₋₁σᵢσᵢ₋₁` — the other word of both rules. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.wHi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BraidSelfOverlap.wHi","kind":"def","line":1907,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1907-L1908","doc":"`σᵢσᵢ₋₁σᵢ` — the shared leading monomial. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuadLeft.quad_bokutShiao_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuadLeft.quad_bokutShiao_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":1845,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1845-L1860","doc":"Bokut–Shiao **at `j = i − 1` only**. `bsWord₂ i' i j = σᵢ₋₁ :: descWord i j`\nputs the extra letter on the left, so for `j < i − 1` the other word is not\n`u'' ++ [σ_z]` and this family does not reach it. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuadLeft.quad_yangBaxter_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuadLeft.quad_yangBaxter_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":1824,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1824-L1843","doc":"Yang–Baxter: `u'' = [σᵢ₋₁, σᵢ]`, `x = i`, `z = i − 1`, `c = −1`. Terms in the\nopposite order to the family's normal form again, hence the coefficientwise\n`hrel`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuadLeft.quad_farComm_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuadLeft.quad_farComm_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":1813,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1813-L1822","doc":"Far-commutation: `u'' = [σⱼ]`, `x = z = i`, `c = 1`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuadLeft.oc_reduces_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuadLeft.oc_reduces_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":1695,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1695-L1802","doc":"**Three steps, to zero.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuadLeft.word_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuadLeft.word_ne","kind":"theorem","line":1680,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1680-L1693","doc":"The leading monomial and the other word have the same length, so length\ncannot separate them; `lc = c ≠ 0` can. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuadLeft.oc_spoly_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuadLeft.oc_spoly_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":1656,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1656-L1678","doc":"**The S-polynomial**, three terms, ambient word already cancelled. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuadLeft.oc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuadLeft.oc","kind":"def","line":1643,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1643-L1654","doc":"The composition of the quadratic rule at `σₓ` with a two-term rule whose\nleading monomial begins with `σₓ`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuad.bokutShiao_quad_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuad.bokutShiao_quad_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":1586,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1586-L1600","doc":"Bokut–Shiao: `u' = descWord i j`, `x = i`, `y = i−1`, `c = 1`. The cyclic form\nis `descWord_cons` — `bsWord₂ i' i j = σᵢ₋₁ :: descWord i j`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuad.yangBaxter_quad_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuad.yangBaxter_quad_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":1565,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1565-L1584","doc":"Yang–Baxter: `u' = [σᵢ, σᵢ₋₁]`, `x = i`, `y = i−1`, `c = −1`. Its two terms\nappear in the opposite order to the family's normal form, which is exactly why\n`hrel` is stated coefficientwise. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuad.farComm_quad_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuad.farComm_quad_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":1554,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1554-L1563","doc":"Far-commutation: `u' = [σᵢ]`, `x = y = j`, `c = 1`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuad.oc_reduces_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuad.oc_reduces_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":1434,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1434-L1546","doc":"**Three steps, to zero.**\n\nStep 1 applies `r` in the context `(σ_y, ε)`, step 2 the quadratic rule at `y` in\nthe context `(ε, u')`, step 3 `r` again in empty context. Only the three\n\"the targeted coefficient is non-zero\" conditions need any word distinguished\nfrom another; every `CoeffEq` holds unconditionally, because the cancellations\nare between *coefficients* and do not care whether the words happen to\ncoincide. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuad.word_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuad.word_ne","kind":"theorem","line":1419,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1419-L1432","doc":"The leading monomial and the other word have the same length, so length\ncannot separate them — but `lc = c ≠ 0` can: were they equal the two terms would\ncancel and the leading coefficient would be `0`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuad.oc_spoly_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuad.oc_spoly_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":1394,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1394-L1417","doc":"**The S-polynomial**, three terms, with the ambient word already cancelled. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuad.oc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.CyclicQuad.oc","kind":"def","line":1376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1376-L1389","doc":"The composition of a two-term rule whose leading monomial ends in `σₓ` with\nthe quadratic rule at `σₓ`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farCommRelation_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farCommRelation_mem","kind":"theorem","line":1364,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1364-L1370","doc":"The far-commutation rule is a rule of the completed system. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yangBaxterRelation_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yangBaxterRelation_mem","kind":"theorem","line":1356,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1356-L1362","doc":"The Yang–Baxter rule is a rule of the completed system. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRelation_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRelation_mem","kind":"theorem","line":1350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1350-L1354","doc":"…and is a rule of the completed system. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRelation_lc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRelation_lc","kind":"theorem","line":1342,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1342-L1348","doc":"The quadratic rule is monic. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.h_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.HeckeParams.h_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":1327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1327-L1340","doc":"`h = q − q⁻¹ ≠ 0`. `q > 0` and `q ≠ 1` are exactly what rules out `q² = 1`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.YangBaxterFarComm.oc_reduces_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.YangBaxterFarComm.oc_reduces_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":1282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1282-L1289","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.YangBaxterFarComm.oc_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.YangBaxterFarComm.oc_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":1259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1259-L1280","doc":"**One step, to zero**, with coefficient `−1` where the Bokut–Shiao version\nuses `+1`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.YangBaxterFarComm.oc_spoly_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.YangBaxterFarComm.oc_spoly_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":1226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1226-L1257","doc":"**The S-polynomial is minus the Bokut–Shiao relation at `j₀`.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.YangBaxterFarComm.oc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.YangBaxterFarComm.oc","kind":"def","line":1214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1214-L1224","doc":"The composition of `yangBaxterRelation i' i` with `farCommRelation i j₀`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.YangBaxterFarComm.descWord_at_pred","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.YangBaxterFarComm.descWord_at_pred","kind":"theorem","line":1209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1209-L1212","doc":"`descWord i (i−1) = σᵢσᵢ₋₁`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarComm.oc_reduces_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarComm.oc_reduces_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":1181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1181-L1188","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarComm.oc_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarComm.oc_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":1159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1159-L1179","doc":"**One step, to zero** — the general form of `refuting_overlap_resolves`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarComm.oc_spoly_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarComm.oc_spoly_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":1124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1124-L1157","doc":"**The S-polynomial is the Bokut–Shiao relation one index lower.** Coefficient\nby coefficient — the ambient word cancels identically, so no word-distinctness\nargument is needed anywhere. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarComm.oc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.BokutShiaoFarComm.oc","kind":"def","line":1111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1111-L1122","doc":"The composition of `bokutShiaoRelation i' i j` with `farCommRelation i j₀`,\noverlapping in the single letter `σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiaoRelation_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiaoRelation_mem","kind":"theorem","line":1095,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1095-L1103","doc":"Every Bokut–Shiao rule really is a rule of the completed system. The `(3,1)`\ninstance is `Completion.bs31_mem`; this is it for all indices. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farCommRelation_lc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farCommRelation_lc","kind":"theorem","line":1086,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1086-L1093","doc":"The far-commutation rule is monic. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiaoRelation_lc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiaoRelation_lc","kind":"theorem","line":1076,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1076-L1084","doc":"The Bokut–Shiao rule is monic: deg-lex picks `bsWord₁`, which carries `+1`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₂_ne_bsWord₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₂_ne_bsWord₁","kind":"theorem","line":1066,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1066-L1074","doc":"The two Bokut–Shiao words are distinct: they differ at their first letter,\n`σᵢ` against `σᵢ₋₁`. `bokutShiaoRelation_lc` needs this to read the leading\ncoefficient off a two-term `ofTerms`, and `monicStep` needs it as `hLR`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_snoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_snoc","kind":"theorem","line":1055,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1055-L1062","doc":"**The snoc lemma**: extending the descending range one index lower appends\nthat letter. Dual to `descWord_cons`, and the only new word identity §4o needs. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.filter_desc_snoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.filter_desc_snoc","kind":"theorem","line":1020,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L1020-L1053","doc":"The mirror of `filter_desc_cons` at the bottom end. `List.finRange n` is\n`Pairwise (· < ·)`, so once the head is `j₀` every later index is at least\n`j = j₀ + 1` and the two predicates agree on the tail; before the head is\nreached both fail, because `a < j₀ < j`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quadSelfOverlap_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quadSelfOverlap_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":983,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L983-L986","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quadSelfOverlap_spoly_isZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quadSelfOverlap_spoly_isZero","kind":"theorem","line":972,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L972-L981","doc":"**The quadratic self-overlap has S-polynomial identically zero** — for every\n`n` and every generator. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quadSelfOverlap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quadSelfOverlap","kind":"def","line":960,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L960-L970","doc":"The composition of the quadratic rule with itself over `σᵢσᵢσᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRelation_coeff_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeRelation_coeff_comm","kind":"theorem","line":945,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L945-L958","doc":"Every monomial of the quadratic relation commutes with `σᵢ`: they are `σᵢσᵢ`,\n`σᵢ` and the empty word, all powers of the one generator. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.inclusion_contexts_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.inclusion_contexts_empty","kind":"theorem","line":909,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L909-L931","doc":"**Every inclusion composition of the completed system has empty contexts.**\n\nNo hypothesis about *which* rules: `decomposition` exhibits `inner.lm` as an\ninfix of `outer.lm`, the antichain forces them equal, and lengths do the rest.\nSo the inclusion half of the Gröbner–Shirshov condition at `n = 4` is entirely\nthe shared-leading-monomial case — `InclusionComposition.spoly_isZero_of_self`\nwhen the two rules coincide, `DegenerateYbBs.ybBsInclusion_spoly_isZero` when\nthey are the Yang–Baxter/Bokut–Shiao pair. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.completedLMSet_four_infix_antichain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.completedLMSet_four_infix_antichain","kind":"theorem","line":904,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L904-L907","doc":"**No leading monomial of the completed system is a proper factor of\nanother.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlapTriples_four_proper_overlap_length_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlapTriples_four_proper_overlap_length_one","kind":"theorem","line":899,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L899-L902","doc":"**Every proper overlap is a single letter.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.bsYbInclusion_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.bsYbInclusion_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":868,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L868-L871","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.ybBsInclusion_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.ybBsInclusion_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":863,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L863-L866","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.bsYbInclusion_spoly_isZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.bsYbInclusion_spoly_isZero","kind":"theorem","line":851,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L851-L861","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.ybBsInclusion_spoly_isZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.ybBsInclusion_spoly_isZero","kind":"theorem","line":839,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L839-L849","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.bsYbInclusion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.bsYbInclusion","kind":"def","line":827,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L827-L837","doc":"…and the other way round. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.ybBsInclusion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.ybBsInclusion","kind":"def","line":815,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L815-L825","doc":"The inclusion composition of the two rules that share a leading monomial. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.bsYbOverlap_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.bsYbOverlap_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":803,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L803-L806","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.ybBsOverlap_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.ybBsOverlap_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":797,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L797-L801","doc":"**The Gröbner–Shirshov obligation for these compositions, discharged.** ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.bsYbOverlap_spoly_isZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.bsYbOverlap_spoly_isZero","kind":"theorem","line":784,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L784-L795","doc":"The other ordering, for the same reason with the signs exchanged. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.ybBsOverlap_spoly_isZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.ybBsOverlap_spoly_isZero","kind":"theorem","line":770,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L770-L782","doc":"**The Yang–Baxter/Bokut–Shiao S-polynomial is zero.** Not \"reduces to zero\" —\nzero. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.bsYbOverlap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.bsYbOverlap","kind":"def","line":758,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L758-L768","doc":"…and the same pair the other way round. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.ybBsOverlap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.ybBsOverlap","kind":"def","line":745,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L745-L756","doc":"The degenerate composition of the two rules that share a leading monomial,\nYang–Baxter first. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.relations_add_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.relations_add_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":730,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L730-L743","doc":"The two relations sum to zero, coefficient by coefficient. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.bokutShiao_lc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.bokutShiao_lc","kind":"theorem","line":720,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L720-L728","doc":"The Bokut–Shiao rule at `j = i − 1` leads with coefficient `+1` on the same\nword — it is oriented the other way round. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.yangBaxter_lc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.yangBaxter_lc","kind":"theorem","line":711,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L711-L718","doc":"The Yang–Baxter rule leads with coefficient `−1`: deg-lex picks the word\nstarting with the larger generator, which is the *subtracted* term. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.ne_of_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs.ne_of_succ","kind":"theorem","line":708,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L708-L709","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlapTriples_four_proper_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlapTriples_four_proper_count","kind":"theorem","line":671,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L671-L675","doc":"The other forty-five have both contexts non-empty. `NotAGSBasis.oc` — the\ncomposition that refutes the uncompleted system — is one of them. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlapTriples_four_degenerate_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlapTriples_four_degenerate_count","kind":"theorem","line":665,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L665-L669","doc":"Thirteen of the fifty-eight are the degenerate self-pairings, one per\nleading monomial: `left = right = []`, `overlap = lm₁ = lm₂`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlapTriples_four_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlapTriples_four_length","kind":"theorem","line":661,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L661-L663","doc":"**Fifty-eight overlap shapes at `n = 4`.** The number the completeness proof\nhas to work through, in place of an estimate. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.completedLMSet_four_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.completedLMSet_four_length","kind":"theorem","line":656,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L656-L659","doc":"…but only thirteen distinct leading monomials. The three lost are exactly the\nYang–Baxter words, which §4j identifies with the Bokut–Shiao rules at\n`j = i − 1`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.completedLMWords_four_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.completedLMWords_four_length","kind":"theorem","line":652,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L652-L654","doc":"Sixteen rules — 4 quadratic, 3 Yang–Baxter, 3 far-commutation, 6\nBokut–Shiao. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.mem_overlapTriples","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.mem_overlapTriples","kind":"theorem","line":630,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L630-L646","doc":"**The bridge.** Any splitting of two leading monomials that meets the\n`OverlapComposition` conditions is in the enumerated list. Stated on words rather\nthan on compositions so that it applies to a composition of *any* two rules with\nthose leading monomials — including two distinct rules leading on the same\nword. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlapTriples","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.overlapTriples","kind":"def","line":615,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L615-L628","doc":"**The overlap shapes** of the completed system at rank `n`: every triple\n`(left, overlap, right)` whose `left ++ overlap` and `overlap ++ right` are both\nleading monomials and whose `overlap` is non-empty.\n\nThe degenerate shapes are deliberately kept. `OverlapComposition` places no\ncondition on `left` or `right`, so `left = right = []` (the two rules lead on the\n*same* word) is a legal composition, and at the three words of §4j it is an\ninhabited one. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompletedRewritingSystem_lm_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompletedRewritingSystem_lm_mem","kind":"theorem","line":589,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L589-L613","doc":"**Soundness of the enumeration**: every rule of the completed system leads on\na word in the list. This is `heckeCompletedRewritingSystem_lm_cases` with the\nexistentials discharged into list membership, which is what makes the overlap\ncount downstream a statement about the actual rule set. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.completedLMSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.completedLMSet","kind":"def","line":584,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L584-L587","doc":"The *distinct* leading monomials. §4j is why this is shorter than\n`completedLMWords`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.completedLMWords","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.completedLMWords","kind":"def","line":579,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L579-L582","doc":"Every leading monomial of the completed system, as an explicit list, with the\nduplicates the four families produce between them still present. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiaoLMs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiaoLMs","kind":"def","line":569,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L569-L577","doc":"Leading monomials of the Bokut–Shiao family, `bsWord₁ i j`.\n\nThe rule is indexed by `(i', i, j)` with `i' + 1 = i` and `j ≤ i'`, but its\nleading monomial depends only on `(i, j)` and the two side conditions collapse to\n`j < i` — so this list has exactly one entry per rule. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farCommLMs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.farCommLMs","kind":"def","line":563,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L563-L567","doc":"Leading monomials of the far-commutation family, `σᵢσⱼ` with `j + 1 < i`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yangBaxterLMs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.yangBaxterLMs","kind":"def","line":556,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L556-L561","doc":"Leading monomials of the Yang–Baxter family, `σⱼσᵢσⱼ` with `j = i + 1`\n(`yangBaxterRelation_lm`: deg-lex puts the larger generator first). ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quadLMs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.quadLMs","kind":"def","line":552,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L552-L554","doc":"Leading monomials of the quadratic family, `σᵢσᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompletedRewritingSystem_lm_ne_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompletedRewritingSystem_lm_ne_nil","kind":"theorem","line":517,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L517-L527","doc":"No rule of the completed system has an empty leading monomial — the\nnon-degeneracy `gs_basis_of_empty_lm` shows is essential, re-established for the\nlarger rule set. The Bokut–Shiao words are never empty: `bsWord₁ i j` ends in\n`σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompletedRewritingSystem_lm_cases","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompletedRewritingSystem_lm_cases","kind":"theorem","line":497,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L497-L515","doc":"**Every rule of `heckeCompletedRewritingSystem` is one of four families**, and\nits leading monomial is the explicit word listed here. The first three cases are\n`heckeRewritingSystem_lm_cases` verbatim, since the completed system keeps every\noriginal rule; the fourth is the Bokut–Shiao family, via the general\n`bokutShiaoRelation_lm`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.mem_heckeCompletedRewritingSystem_rules","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.mem_heckeCompletedRewritingSystem_rules","kind":"theorem","line":469,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L469-L495","doc":"**Every rule of `heckeCompletedRewritingSystem` is one of four relations**,\nwith its indices and its side condition. The inversion of `heckeRelation_mem` and\nits three siblings, and the rule-level strengthening of\n`heckeCompletedRewritingSystem_lm_cases` below. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiao_lm_eq_yangBaxter_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiao_lm_eq_yangBaxter_lm","kind":"theorem","line":443,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L443-L449","doc":"Both rules lead on `σᵢσᵢ₋₁σᵢ` — deg-lex ranks `σᵢ` above `σᵢ₋₁`, so the word\nstarting with the larger generator wins, exactly as in `yangBaxterRelation_lm`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiaoRelation_at_pred","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiaoRelation_at_pred","kind":"theorem","line":431,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L431-L441","doc":"**The Bokut–Shiao rule at `j = i − 1` is the Yang–Baxter rule**, up to the\nsign convention: its relation is `σᵢσᵢ₋₁σᵢ − σᵢ₋₁σᵢσᵢ₋₁`, and\n`yangBaxterRelation i' i` is the negative of that.\n\nSo the family really does extend the presentation rather than sit beside it, and\nthe two rules share a leading monomial (`bokutShiao_lm_eq_yangBaxter_lm`). ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₂_at_pred","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₂_at_pred","kind":"theorem","line":421,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L421-L429","doc":"…and the right one is `σᵢ₋₁σᵢσᵢ₋₁`.\n\nNote this needs **no** relation between `i'` and `i`: `bsWord₂ i' i j` is\n`σᵢ₋₁ σᵢ` followed by `descWord i' j`, so at `j = i'` the tail collapses by\n`descWord_self` whatever `i` is. It is the *left* word that needs `i' + 1 = i`,\nbecause that is where `descWord_cons` is used. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₁_at_pred","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₁_at_pred","kind":"theorem","line":415,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L415-L419","doc":"At `j = i − 1` the left Bokut–Shiao word is the braid word `σᵢσᵢ₋₁σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_self","kind":"theorem","line":409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L409-L413","doc":"The descending word from `i` down to `i` is the single letter `σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.filter_desc_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.filter_desc_self","kind":"theorem","line":382,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L382-L407","doc":"The filter that defines `descWord i i` keeps exactly the one index `i`:\neverything after `i` in a `Pairwise (· < ·)` list exceeds it, and everything\nbefore it is below. Same shape as `filter_desc_cons`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiaoRelation_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiaoRelation_lm","kind":"theorem","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L355-L373","doc":"**The general leading monomial** `lm(bokutShiaoRelation i' i j) = bsWord₁ i j`.\n\nBoth words have length `|descWord i' j| + 2` — visible from `bsWord₁_cons`, with\nno length computation — and deg-lex ranks `σᵢ` above `σᵢ₋₁`, so the word starting\nwith `σᵢ` is the larger. Compare `Completion.bs31_lm`, which is this at\n`(i', i, j) = (2, 3, 1)` and was proved by `fin_cases` before this existed. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₁_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₁_cons","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L347-L353","doc":"Both Bokut–Shiao words in cons form, sharing a visible tail. This is what\nmakes the leading-monomial comparison a one-letter lex step with no length\narithmetic: `σᵢ :: (w ++ [σᵢ])` against `σᵢ₋₁ :: σᵢ :: w`, same `w`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord_cons","kind":"theorem","line":338,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L338-L345","doc":"**The cons lemma**: dropping the top index drops the first letter. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.filter_desc_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.filter_desc_cons","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L296-L336","doc":"`List.finRange n` is `Pairwise (· < ·)`, so once the head is `i` every later\nindex exceeds it and both filters annihilate the tail; before the head is reached\nthe two predicates agree, because `a < i = i' + 1` forces `a ≤ i'`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.refuting_overlap_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.refuting_overlap_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L260-L286","doc":"**The overlap that refutes the uncompleted system resolves in the completed\none** — one step, to zero.\n\nThis is the Gröbner–Shirshov condition for this composition, and it is strictly\nstronger than `spoly_not_isNormalForm_completed`: not merely \"reducible\" but\n\"reduces to zero\". Contrast `NotAGSBasis.spoly_isNormalForm`, which is the same\nS-polynomial against `heckeRewritingSystem` and cannot be reduced at all. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.spoly_add_relation_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.spoly_add_relation_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L242-L258","doc":"The S-polynomial and the Bokut–Shiao relation cancel coefficient by\ncoefficient. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.three_words_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.three_words_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L233-L240","doc":"`w₁`, `w₂` and the ambient word `σ₃σ₂σ₃σ₁` are three distinct words. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.bs31_lc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.bs31_lc","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L228-L231","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.spoly_not_isNormalForm_completed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.spoly_not_isNormalForm_completed","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L201-L213","doc":"**The completed system reduces the S-polynomial that refutes the\nuncompleted one.** `w₂` carries a non-zero coefficient and is the leading\nmonomial of `bs31`, hence an infix of itself — so the S-polynomial is not a\nnormal form, and the obstruction of §4e is gone.\n\nContrast `NotAGSBasis.spoly_isNormalForm`, which is the same S-polynomial\nagainst `heckeRewritingSystem`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.spoly_coeff_w₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.spoly_coeff_w₂","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L186-L199","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.bs31_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.bs31_mem","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L172-L177","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.bs31_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.bs31_lm","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L159-L170","doc":"`lm(bs31) = σ₃σ₂σ₁σ₃`. Both words have length 4, and deg-lex ranks `σ₃`\nabove `σ₂`, so the word starting with `σ₃` is the larger. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.bs31_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.bs31_relation","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L152-L157","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.bsWord₂_231","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.bsWord₂_231","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L149-L150","doc":"Its right-hand word is `w₁`, the other one. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.bsWord₁_31","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.bsWord₁_31","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L146-L147","doc":"Its left-hand word is `w₂`, one of the two words §4e shows irreducible. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.bs31","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.Completion.bs31","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L142-L144","doc":"The Bokut–Shiao rule at `(i, j) = (3, 1)`: `σ₃σ₂σ₁σ₃ → σ₂σ₃σ₂σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompletedRewritingSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.heckeCompletedRewritingSystem","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L116-L131","doc":"The Hecke rewriting system **completed** with the Bokut–Shiao family.\nEvery rule of `heckeRewritingSystem` is kept, so every membership and\nleading-monomial fact proved there still applies verbatim; the new block adds\n`bokutShiaoRelation i' i j` for each `i' + 1 = i` and `j ≤ i'`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiaoRelation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bokutShiaoRelation","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L106-L114","doc":"**The Bokut–Shiao rule** `σᵢσᵢ₋₁⋯σⱼσᵢ − σᵢ₋₁σᵢσᵢ₋₁⋯σⱼ`, with `i'` standing\nfor `i − 1`. Undeformed: see the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₂","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L102-L104","doc":"`σᵢ₋₁ σᵢ σᵢ₋₁ ⋯ σⱼ` — the right-hand side. `i'` stands for `i − 1`. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.bsWord₁","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L97-L100","doc":"`σᵢ σᵢ₋₁ ⋯ σⱼ σᵢ` — the left-hand side of the Bokut–Shiao rule, and (for\n`j < i`) its leading monomial. ","signatureChunk":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.descWord","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/HeckeCompletion.lean#L90-L95","doc":"The descending word `σᵢ σᵢ₋₁ ⋯ σⱼ`, built by filtering `List.finRange n`\nso that no index arithmetic is needed. Empty when `i < j`. ","signatureChunk":1}]}